;BRA-20/0020;Fostering science-based and participatory governance processes to face marin litter in Brazil;BRA-2053;Sustainable Oceans;B;2025;27.05.2025;Actual;400 000;0;NOK;2021;2025;FUNBIO;Grant;4130;Brasilia;0159;0159.77;0159.77.111;Latin-Amerika og Karibia - nasjonale tiltak;Brazil;JAMB;Jaegger, Mona Berg;;03;;06.12.2021;Funbio - Fundo Brasileiro para a Biodiversidade;Funbio - Fundo Brasileiro para a Biodiversidade;NGO Local;I;Project- and programme grant;Bilateral;Project-type interventions;41020;410;General environmental protection;20;Biosphere protection;;-;-;-;-;-;Main;-;-;Main;-;-;-;-;-;-;-;The project supports the development of tools and a strategic plan to monitor and combat marine litter in a number of coastal states in Brazil, also potentially to include neighbouring countries in the region. The project will foster science-based and participatory governance processes to raise awarness and secure committment to monitor and tackle marine litter at political level as well as within academia/ research institutions, NGOs and with the civil society. ;The project is a scale-up based on the positive results of BRA-18/0034, which supported the first public policy of its kind in the country. In addition, the project was included in the UNEP Stocktake of Actions on Marine Plastic Litter and Microplastics demanded by UNEA Resolution 4/6 to support the discussion at UNEA 5. ;
;BRA-23/0002;Support to Transparency International Brazil;BRA-2052;Research and Policy Making, Transparency and HR;B;2025;26.06.2025;Actual;1 850 000;0;BRL  ;2023;2026;Associacao Transparencia e Integridade;Grant;4130;Brasilia;0159;0159.77;0159.77.111;Latin-Amerika og Karibia - nasjonale tiltak;Brazil;JAMB;Jaegger, Mona Berg;;03;;01.08.2023;Transparency International - local office;Transparency International - local office;NGO Local;I;Project- and programme grant;Bilateral;Core support to NGOs, other private bodies, PPPs and research institutes;15113;151;Government and civil society, general;13;Anti-corruption organisations and institutions ;;-;-;-;-;-;Significant;-;Main;-;Significant;-;-;-;-;-;-;Support to Transparency International-Chapter in Brazil. Support to the TI Brazil infrastructure (Operations Office, Advocacy and Anticorruption Knowledge Centre). Support to a strong permanent presence in Brazil, in order to contribute to the fight against corruption, with special focus on local governance, business and environment. Main target groups are the Brazilian civil society, government, private sector and academia, and BRICS, Mercosur, G20 and Global South.;;
;BRA-23/0002;Support to Transparency International Brazil;BRA-2052;Research and Policy Making, Transparency and HR;B;2025;01.10.2025;Planned;550 000;0;;2023;2026;Associacao Transparencia e Integridade;;4130;Brasilia;0159;0159.77;0159.77.111;Latin-Amerika og Karibia - nasjonale tiltak;Brazil;JAMB;Jaegger, Mona Berg;;03;;01.08.2023;Transparency International - local office;Transparency International - local office;NGO Local;I;Project- and programme grant;Bilateral;Core support to NGOs, other private bodies, PPPs and research institutes;15113;151;Government and civil society, general;13;Anti-corruption organisations and institutions ;;-;-;-;-;-;Significant;-;Main;-;Significant;-;-;-;-;-;-;Support to Transparency International-Chapter in Brazil. Support to the TI Brazil infrastructure (Operations Office, Advocacy and Anticorruption Knowledge Centre). Support to a strong permanent presence in Brazil, in order to contribute to the fight against corruption, with special focus on local governance, business and environment. Main target groups are the Brazilian civil society, government, private sector and academia, and BRICS, Mercosur, G20 and Global South.;;
