;BRA-25/0008;Support Joar Nango at 36th SP Bienal;BRA-2038;Culture, Private sector and Public Diplomacy  ;B;2025;18.07.2025;Actual;40 000;0;BRL  ;2025;2025;Fundacao Bienal de Sao Paulo;Grant;4130;Brasilia;0115;0115.70;0115.70.112;Kultur- og informasjonsformål - ute/stasjonene;Brazil;U14004;Brauer Goncalves, Joana;;02;;16.06.2025;Undefined (Fundacao Bienal de São Paulo);Undefined (Fundacao Bienal de São Paulo);NGO Local;III;Small-scale grant;Bilateral;Project-type interventions;16061;160;Other social infrastructure and services;61;Culture and cultural diversity;;-;-;-;-;-;Significant;-;Significant;-;-;-;Significant;Significant;-;-;-;Support Sámi artist Joar Nango's participation at the 36th São Paulo Bienal. Project also funded by OCA. Joar Nango’s project is directly connected to urgent global issues. It offers a unique cultural exchange through an immersive installation that brings together Sámi and Brazilian Indigenous architectural traditions. This initiative addresses critical themes such as ecology, cultural preservation, and historical reparation, encouraging visitors to engage with contemporary art in a dynamic and participatory way. In other words, the project is expected to generate meaningful social impact, with strong relevance to the Brazilian and global context.;;
;BRA-25/0009;Ståle Wig to Brazil;BRA-2038;Culture, Private sector and Public Diplomacy  ;B;2025;23.09.2025;Actual;15 000;0;NOK;2025;2025;Ståle Wig;Grant;4130;Brasilia;0115;0115.70;0115.70.112;Kultur- og informasjonsformål - ute/stasjonene;Brazil;U14004;Brauer Goncalves, Joana;;02;;08.09.2025;Undefined (Ståle Wig);Undefined (Ståle Wig);NGO Norwegian;III;Small-scale grant;Bilateral;Project-type interventions;16061;160;Other social infrastructure and services;61;Culture and cultural diversity;;-;-;-;-;-;-;-;Main;-;-;-;-;-;-;-;-;Support Ståle Wig's trip to BR for book launch Havana Táxi. In partnership with the General-Consulate in Rio, Buzz Editora, Porto Alegre Book Fair and translator Guilherme Braga. Ståle will visit São Paulo, Rio, Porto Alegre and Canoas.The Norwegian author Ståle Wig is travelling to Brazil to launch the Portuguese translation of his book, “Havanna Taxi: Liv og løgn på det nye Cuba”. The program proposal encompasses several types of activities, from book fairs to academic debates and media interviews. The program is expected to raise awareness of contemporary Cuban society through the book Havana Taxi, fostering dialogue between Norwegian and Brazilian audiences. It is expected to strengthen academic and cultural exchange, contribute to building networks with universities, writers, and translators, and expand the book’s readership in Brazil.;;
;BRA-25/0009;Ståle Wig to Brazil;BRA-2038;Culture, Private sector and Public Diplomacy  ;B;2025;30.09.2025;Actual;7 888;0;NOK;2025;2025;Ståle Wig;Grant;4130;Brasilia;0115;0115.70;0115.70.112;Kultur- og informasjonsformål - ute/stasjonene;Brazil;U14004;Brauer Goncalves, Joana;;02;;08.09.2025;Undefined (Ståle Wig);Undefined (Ståle Wig);NGO Norwegian;III;Small-scale grant;Bilateral;Project-type interventions;16061;160;Other social infrastructure and services;61;Culture and cultural diversity;;-;-;-;-;-;-;-;Main;-;-;-;-;-;-;-;-;Support Ståle Wig's trip to BR for book launch Havana Táxi. In partnership with the General-Consulate in Rio, Buzz Editora, Porto Alegre Book Fair and translator Guilherme Braga. Ståle will visit São Paulo, Rio, Porto Alegre and Canoas.The Norwegian author Ståle Wig is travelling to Brazil to launch the Portuguese translation of his book, “Havanna Taxi: Liv og løgn på det nye Cuba”. The program proposal encompasses several types of activities, from book fairs to academic debates and media interviews. The program is expected to raise awareness of contemporary Cuban society through the book Havana Taxi, fostering dialogue between Norwegian and Brazilian audiences. It is expected to strengthen academic and cultural exchange, contribute to building networks with universities, writers, and translators, and expand the book’s readership in Brazil.;;
