;CHN-22/0011;Sino-Norwegian project on methane from livestock production and waste management (ChiNorCH4);CHN-2148;Climate Change;B;2025;01.11.2025;Planned;1 560 000;0;;2024;2027;Miljødirektoratet;;4070;Beijing/China;0159;0159.76;0159.76.111;Asia - nasjonale tiltak;China;YILI;Liu, Yinglang;;03;;29.04.2024;China Ministry of Commerce;China Ministry of Commerce;Governments/Ministries in developing countries;I;Project- and programme grant;Bilateral;Project-type interventions;41010;410;General environmental protection;10;Environmental policy and administrative management;;-;-;-;-;-;Main;-;-;-;-;-;Significant;-;-;-;-;The project's main goal is to develop comprehensive strategies for controlling methane emissions in the waste treatment and livestock production sectors in northern China, thereby contributing to China achieving its 2060 carbon neutrality goal and commitments under the Paris Agreement. Its main implementing institutions are Chinese Research Academy of Environmental Sciences (CRAES), a research institute affiliated with China's Ministry of Ecology and Environment, and Norwegian Environment Agency (NEA), a technical support unit to Norway's Ministry of Climate and Environmentt.  ;;
