;CHN-22/0013;Sinograin III;CHN-2152;Policy development and capacity building;B;2025;26.08.2025;Actual;1 150 000;0;NOK;2023;2027;NIBIO - NORSK INSTITUTT FOR BIOØKONOMI;Grant;4070;Beijing/China;0159;0159.76;0159.76.111;Asia - nasjonale tiltak;China;U17671;Chen, Tingting;;03;;31.10.2023;NIBIO - Norsk institutt for bioøkonomi;NIBIO - Norsk institutt for bioøkonomi;Norwegian public sector;I;Project- and programme grant;Bilateral;Project-type interventions;31161;311;Agriculture;61;Food crop production;;-;-;-;-;-;Significant;Significant;-;-;Main;-;-;-;-;-;-;Sinograin III builds on the achievements and experiences of the Sinograin I and Sinograin II projects, aiming to contribute to the UN SDGs by widely implementing precision agriculture technologies and application of “waste-to-value” biochar products to achieve sustainable food production with minimized GHG emission, improve soil fertility and promote green growth/zero waste in modern agriculture in China. The project will be implemented by NIBIO.;;
;CHN-22/0014;SINOPLAST II, Sino-Norwegian cooperation on capacity building for reducing plastic and microplastic pollution;CHN-2152;Policy development and capacity building;B;2025;18.11.2025;Actual;2 000 000;0;NOK;2024;2027;Tsinghua University;Grant;4070;Beijing/China;0159;0159.76;0159.76.111;Asia - nasjonale tiltak;China;U17671;Chen, Tingting;;03;;29.04.2024;China Ministry of Commerce;BCRC China - Basel Convention Regional Centre for Asia and Pacific in China;Governments/Ministries in developing countries;I;Project- and programme grant;Bilateral;Project-type interventions;41020;410;General environmental protection;20;Biosphere protection;;-;-;-;-;-;Main;Significant;-;-;-;-;-;-;-;-;-;SINOPLAST II aims to develop necessary tools to improve the capacities of plastic management in China and thus increase China’s preparedness for upcoming international agreement on plastics. The project is implemented by the Ministry of Ecology and Environment of the People's Republic of China through the Basel Convention Regional Centre for Asia and the Pacific in China (BCRC China). The Norwegian Institute of Water Research (NIVA) is leading the project on the Norwegian side with support from the Norwegian Environment Agency (NEA). The project includes measurement of female participants.;;
