;CIV-24/0001;Equal Access International - Résilience pour la Paix;RAF-3025;Regional Security and Peacekeeping Cooperation in West-Africa;B;2025;15.07.2025;Actual;1 000 000;0;NOK;2025;2026;Association Resilience pour la paix;Grant;4015;Accra;0159;0159.75;0159.75.111;Afrika - nasjonale tiltak;Cote D'Ivoire;U15750;Nakkim, Vilde Larsen;;03;;30.06.2025;R4P - Association Resilience pour la Paix;R4P - Association Resilience pour la Paix;NGO Local;I;Project- and programme grant;Bilateral;Contributions to specific-purpose programmes and funds managed by implementing partners;15150;151;Government and civil society, general;50;Democratic participation and civil society;;-;-;-;-;-;-;-;-;-;-;-;-;-;-;-;-;The overall goal is to strengthen evidence-based policy responses to prevent violent extremism (VE) in northern Côte d’Ivoire. By expanding R4P’s Development & Resilience Index to Violence Extremism (DRIVE) – an index which captures communities’ stress factors and resilience capacity – R4P will provide vital information to local, regional, national and international stakeholders to improve policy responses and projects. They will offer individualized support to various stakeholder groups to better grasp findings, understand analyses, and ultimately find ways to transform research into action.;;
;CIV-24/0001;Equal Access International - Résilience pour la Paix;RAF-3025;Regional Security and Peacekeeping Cooperation in West-Africa;B;2025;10.09.2025;Planned;1 000 000;0;;2025;2026;Association Resilience pour la paix;;4015;Accra;0159;0159.75;0159.75.111;Afrika - nasjonale tiltak;Cote D'Ivoire;U15750;Nakkim, Vilde Larsen;;03;;30.06.2025;R4P - Association Resilience pour la Paix;R4P - Association Resilience pour la Paix;NGO Local;I;Project- and programme grant;Bilateral;Contributions to specific-purpose programmes and funds managed by implementing partners;15150;151;Government and civil society, general;50;Democratic participation and civil society;;-;-;-;-;-;-;-;-;-;-;-;-;-;-;-;-;The overall goal is to strengthen evidence-based policy responses to prevent violent extremism (VE) in northern Côte d’Ivoire. By expanding R4P’s Development & Resilience Index to Violence Extremism (DRIVE) – an index which captures communities’ stress factors and resilience capacity – R4P will provide vital information to local, regional, national and international stakeholders to improve policy responses and projects. They will offer individualized support to various stakeholder groups to better grasp findings, understand analyses, and ultimately find ways to transform research into action.;;
