;COL-19/0009;Community Security Observatories: A commitment by the territories;COL-2039;COLOMBIA - Agreements initiated from 2019;B;2025;21.11.2025;Planned;1 500 000;0;;2019;2025;Fundacion Paz y Reconciliacion;;6150;Bogota;0151;0151.70;0151.70.111;Fred og forsoning, kan overføres;Colombia;U18241;Fernandez Caviedes, Laura;;03;;10.06.2019;Pares - Fundacion Paz y Reconciliacion;Pares - Fundacion Paz y Reconciliacion;NGO Local;I;Project- and programme grant;Bilateral;Project-type interventions;15220;152;Conflict prevention and resolution, peace and security;20;Civilian peace-building, conflict prevention and resolution;;-;-;-;-;-;-;Significant;Main;-;-;-;-;-;-;-;-;The project’s main objective is to strengthen the capacities of communities heavily affected by war through the design, implementation and sustainability of Community Security Observatories that will be a space of convergence for territorial organizations in four conflict affected regions in Colombia.;;
;COL-19/0011;Conversatorios (Dialogue spaces) between State Security Forces and Civil;COL-2039;COLOMBIA - Agreements initiated from 2019;B;2025;17.06.2025;Actual;1 709 478;0;NOK;2019;2026;Social Development Group;Grant;6150;Bogota;0151;0151.70;0151.70.111;Fred og forsoning, kan overføres;Colombia;U15531;Bedoya Pardo, Estefania;;03;;21.06.2019;Social Development Group;Social Development Group;NGO Local;I;Project- and programme grant;Bilateral;Project-type interventions;15220;152;Conflict prevention and resolution, peace and security;20;Civilian peace-building, conflict prevention and resolution;;-;-;-;-;-;-;-;Main;-;-;-;-;-;-;-;-;This project is the continuation of previous efforts to strengthening the Colombian Armed Forces' willingness and abilities to actively participate in peacebuilding in Colombia. The main objective of this project is to achieve better levels of trust and communication between State's security forces and civil society both at national level and regional level

;The previous project with the partner (COL-18/0011) had a climate change and deforestation component, but these activities are not included in the new phase. ;
;COL-19/0019;Supporting Transitional Justice Initiatives to Advance Accountability;COL-2039;COLOMBIA - Agreements initiated from 2019;B;2025;17.06.2025;Actual;3 813 906;0;NOK;2019;2025;Centro International para la Justicia Transicional;Grant;6150;Bogota;0151;0151.70;0151.70.111;Fred og forsoning, kan overføres;Colombia;U15531;Bedoya Pardo, Estefania;;03;;25.10.2019;ICTJ - International Centre for Transitional Justice;ICTJ - International Centre for Transitional Justice;NGO International;II;General funding grant;Bilateral;Core support to NGOs, other private bodies, PPPs and research institutes;15130;151;Government and civil society, general;30;Legal and judicial development;;-;-;-;-;-;-;Significant;Main;-;-;-;-;-;-;-;-;Objective: Transitional justice processes in Colombia are implemented in a way that advances accountability of all actors to the internal armed conflict and the fulfillment of victims’ rights. ICTJ will work closely with a range of state actors and civil society in accordance with ICTJ’s annual stakeholder analysis. These will include the SJP, TC and Search Unit, judicial operators, LGBTI, women’s and victims’ organizations, former combatants, and corporate and alternative media.  ;First core support to ICTJ Colombia from the Embassy in Bogota. ICTJ has been a key partner to the Embassy for many years and it is consider a strategic actor in Colombia's transitional context.;
;COL-19/0019;Supporting Transitional Justice Initiatives to Advance Accountability;COL-2039;COLOMBIA - Agreements initiated from 2019;B;2025;10.11.2025;Planned;3 000 000;0;;2019;2025;Centro International para la Justicia Transicional;;6150;Bogota;0151;0151.70;0151.70.111;Fred og forsoning, kan overføres;Colombia;U15531;Bedoya Pardo, Estefania;;03;;25.10.2019;ICTJ - International Centre for Transitional Justice;ICTJ - International Centre for Transitional Justice;NGO International;II;General funding grant;Bilateral;Core support to NGOs, other private bodies, PPPs and research institutes;15130;151;Government and civil society, general;30;Legal and judicial development;;-;-;-;-;-;-;Significant;Main;-;-;-;-;-;-;-;-;Objective: Transitional justice processes in Colombia are implemented in a way that advances accountability of all actors to the internal armed conflict and the fulfillment of victims’ rights. ICTJ will work closely with a range of state actors and civil society in accordance with ICTJ’s annual stakeholder analysis. These will include the SJP, TC and Search Unit, judicial operators, LGBTI, women’s and victims’ organizations, former combatants, and corporate and alternative media.  ;First core support to ICTJ Colombia from the Embassy in Bogota. ICTJ has been a key partner to the Embassy for many years and it is consider a strategic actor in Colombia's transitional context.;
;COL-20/0005;Building territory, culture and identity for peace – Phase III;COL-2040;COLOMBIA - Agreements initiated in 2020 in Bogota;B;2025;24.07.2025;Actual;3 957 000;0;NOK;2020;2025;FLYKTNINGEHJELPEN CO;Grant;6150;Bogota;0151;0151.70;0151.70.111;Fred og forsoning, kan overføres;Colombia;U17893;De Reyes Lanfranco, Ricardo;;03;;27.03.2020;Flyktninghjelpen;Flyktninghjelpen;NGO Norwegian;I;Project- and programme grant;Bilateral;Project-type interventions;15220;152;Conflict prevention and resolution, peace and security;20;Civilian peace-building, conflict prevention and resolution;;-;-;-;-;-;-;Significant;Main;-;-;-;-;-;-;-;-;The project will be carried out by NRC and Fundación Solidaria Arquidiocesana in four departments at the Pacific Coast (Nariño, Cauca, Chocó and Antioquia). The project seeks to strengthen the capacities and initiatives of the communities and ethno-territorial organisations in the Colombian Pacific region, in order to respond adequately to the humanitarian crisis in this area. Simultaneously, the agreement aims to strengthen local conflict resolution mechanisms and capacity building of ethnic-territorial organisations and social leaders to exercise and protect their ethnic/territorial rights. The project will promote indigenous and Afro Colombian women’s leadership in peace building initiatives and promote gender equality in ethnic communities of the Pacific region.;;
;COL-20/0006;Transitioning to a rainbow peace: LGBTI people building peace in Colombia;COL-2040;COLOMBIA - Agreements initiated in 2020 in Bogota;B;2025;20.11.2025;Planned;1 216 302;0;;2020;2026;CORPORACION CARIBE AFIRMATIVO;;6150;Bogota;0152;0152.70;0152.70.111;Menneskerettigheter;Colombia;U16928;Torres Jaramillo, Juan Mauricio;;03;;08.04.2020;Caribe Afirmativo;Caribe Afirmativo;NGO Local;I;Project- and programme grant;Bilateral;Project-type interventions;15160;151;Government and civil society, general;60;Human rights;;-;-;-;-;-;-;Main;Main;-;-;-;-;-;-;-;-;The project will contribute to the effective application of the gender approach in the implementation of the Peace Agreement (PA) by advancing processes of investigation and advocacy before the bodies created within the framework of transitional justice. The objective is to increase the participation of LGBTI people in the implementation of the PA by 1) recognition by JEP of bias-motivated violence against LGBTI people

;;
;COL-22/0004;Coastal communities’ welfare through Ocean Economy business models;QZA-0720;Fisk for utvikling;B;2025;15.08.2025;Actual;1 347 109;0;NOK;2022;2025;Conservation International;Grant;300514;KNN-HAV Seksjon for hav;0162;0162.71;0162.71.112;Fisk for utvikling;Colombia;NORAD-SIKI;Kihl, Sigurd;2100570;03;;03.05.2022;CI – Conservation International;CI – Conservation International;NGO International;I;Project- and programme grant;Bilateral;Project-type interventions;31320;313;Fishing;20;Fishery development;;-;-;-;-;-;Significant;Significant;-;-;-;-;Main;Main;-;-;-;The desired impact of the project “Coastal communities’ welfare through Ocean Economy business models” is that Coastal and fisherfolk communities’ have reduced their poverty conditions by implementing ocean economy based solutions. The project seeks to support decision makers' knowledge and awareness about the importance of improving the resilience and adaptive capacity of local communities against negative impacts of climate change and support integrated mangrove management and mangrove restoration programs through Conservation Agreement. The project seeks to foster gender equality and women empowerment in grassroots communities by promoting women’s associations, strengthening their leadership, and create economic opportunities for women by including them as part of the value chains.;;
