;ETH-23/0005;ABRONET: Restoring cohesion in conflict affected communities in Ethiopia;ETH-3105;Ethiopia Peace and Reconciliation;B;2025;09.10.2025;Actual;4 000 000;0;NOK;2023;2025;Norwegian Church Aid - Norway;Grant;4014;Addis Abeba/Ethiopia;0151;0151.70;0151.70.111;Fred og forsoning, kan overføres;Ethiopia;U17556;Tønnesen, Kristoffer Auestad;;03;;04.12.2023;Kirkens Nødhjelp;Kirkens Nødhjelp;NGO Norwegian;I;Project- and programme grant;Bilateral;Project-type interventions;15220;152;Conflict prevention and resolution, peace and security;20;Civilian peace-building, conflict prevention and resolution;;-;-;-;-;-;-;Significant;Significant;-;-;-;-;-;-;-;-;Promotion of peace and social cohesion through engagement with faith-based actors in conflict affected areas in Ethiopia – particularly directed towards hotspots in Oromia, Amhara, Afar, Tigray, Gambella, Sidama and areas formerly part of SNNPR. The project focuses on grassroots peacebuilding addressing intercommunal violence in hotspots in Ethiopia. An important aim of the project is to build on religious actors (women, men, and youth) and local human resources (women, men and youth) in the conflict contexts to enable and support them in promoting social cohesion and reconciliation in their own conflict contexts. The overall goal is that community members in conflict affected areas in Ethiopia enjoy peaceful coexistence and intercommunal collaboration.;;
