;GHA-25/0001;The Ghana Anti-Disinformation Coalition Project;GHA-2053;Human Rights Ghana;A;2025;30.11.2025;Planned;1 000 000;0;;2025;2028;Pen Plus Bytes;;4015;Accra;0159;0159.75;0159.75.111;Afrika - nasjonale tiltak;Ghana;U18496;Nartey, Samuel Kofi;;03;;;Undefined (PEN Plus Bytes);Undefined (PEN Plus Bytes);NGO Local;I;Project- and programme grant;Bilateral;Project-type interventions;15153;151;Government and civil society, general;53;Media and free flow of information;;-;-;-;-;-;-;Significant;Main;-;-;-;-;-;-;-;-;The Project seeks to address that urgent gap by building and strengthening a national coalition of stakeholders committed to collaboratively combating disinformation in Ghana. By bringing together diverse expertise and resources, the initiative aims to ensure that efforts to counter false information are continuous, resilient, and locally grounded. The Project’s core goal is to foster an informed citizenry through enhanced coalition building, AI Driven digital fact-checking marketplace platform, supportive policy frameworks, and empowered community and grassroots radios which will serve as trusted information hubs. The collective impact of this work will contribute meaningfully to good governance, social cohesion, and democratic resilience in Ghana.;;
