;INS-24/0005;Strengthening the Capacity of Judiciary in Handling Environmental Land-Grabbing Cases;INS-2160;Human rights ;B;2025;28.10.2025;Actual;500 000;0;NOK;2024;2027;Lembaga Kajian dan Advokasi Independensi Peradilan;Grant;4330;Jakarta/Indonesia;0152;0152.70;0152.70.111;Menneskerettigheter;Indonesia;U16269;Widani, Apriline;;03;;28.11.2024;LeIP - Indonesian Institute for Independent Judiciary;LeIP - Indonesian Institute for Independent Judiciary;NGO Local;I;Project- and programme grant;Bilateral;Project-type interventions;15130;151;Government and civil society, general;30;Legal and judicial development;;-;-;-;-;-;Significant;-;Significant;-;Significant;-;-;-;-;-;-;The project's expected effects are strengthened capacity of judiciary in applying human rights principles when handling administrative lawsuits involving land-grabbing and the protection of the environment. The outcomes are: 1) Accessible and comprehensive reference on administrative court decisions over environmental land-grabbing cases, and 2) Enhanced capacity of administrative court judges and legal aid organizations in applying human rights principles in environmental land-grabbing cases. The outpus are 1) Research report on the principles and practices of human rights protection on land-grabbing cases in administrative court decisions, 2) Human rights training module for administrative court judges, 3) Human rights training for administrative court judges, and 4) Training module on human rights and land-grabbing lawsuits for legal aid organizations. ;In implementing the project, LeIP will collaborate with the Norwegian Centre for Human Rights and the Centre for Human Rights and International Justice at Stanford University.;
