;MAR-23/0002;Promoting Best Practices in the State Response to Violence against Women: Mobilization, Monitoring and Advocacy;MAR-2008;Project support;B;2025;27.05.2025;Actual;376 000;0;NOK;2023;2026;Mobilising for Rights Associates;Grant;4550;Rabat;0152;0152.70;0152.70.114;Kvinners rettigheter;Morocco;U14521;Vevatne, Silje Samanthi;;03;;21.11.2023;MRA - Mobilising for Rights Associates;MRA - Mobilising for Rights Associates;NGO International;I;Project- and programme grant;Bilateral;Contributions to specific-purpose programmes and funds managed by implementing partners;15180;151;Government and civil society, general;80;Ending violence against women and girls;;-;-;-;-;-;-;Main;-;-;-;-;-;-;-;-;-;The project aims to improve the State response to gender-based violence against women (GBV) and support anticipated law reforms on women’s rights. The four-pronged strategy will (a) conduct grassroots level mobilization and prevention activities among women, (b) strengthen local systems among justice, law enforcement and health sector actors to respond to GBV, (c) monitor the justice system response in women’s rights cases by collecting and analyzing a diversity of court decisions, and (d) conduct national level advocacy to government and elected officials for reforms to the Penal and Family codes and for support of a draft global treaty to end GBV. ;;
