;The application describes three phases, Phase I: 2024 Presidential Elections and EU referendum, Phase II: 2025 Parliamentary Elections and Phase III: 2026-2028, General Local Elections. The total budget for the three phases is set to USD 9,323,604 (ca. NOK 102 million). This agreement supports phases I and II, with a total budget of USD 3,378,893 (ca. NOK 37 million) – of which Norwegian support is requested for USD 2,444,172 or 72% of the total. Should Norway decide to extend support into phase III, a new assessment should be prepared. ;
;MDA-24/0003;IMS - Moldova Media Information Integrity and Democracy (M-MIIND);MDA-0001;Moldova;B;2025;08.08.2025;Actual;5 000 000;0;NOK;2024;2025;International Media Support;Grant;300540;UKR-NANSEN Avdeling for Nansen-programmet for Ukraina;0159;0159.73;0159.73.111;Ukraina og naboland;Moldova;NORAD-U18079;Wågen, Anna;2401365;03;;10.10.2024;IMS - International Media Support;IMS - International Media Support;NGO International;I;Project- and programme grant;Bilateral;Project-type interventions;15153;151;Government and civil society, general;53;Media and free flow of information;;-;-;-;-;-;-;Significant;Main;-;-;-;-;-;-;-;-;The M-MIIND programme proposes a collaborative approach between independent media to safeguard inclusive democratic dialogue in Moldova. The Programme seeks to support independent media across the country through capacity building and financial support to ensure that the Moldovan population from all segments of society have access to independent information and make informed decisions on issues of public interest regardless of their gender, ethnicity or language. The M-MIIND programme entails supporting projects from independent media – through capacity building and financial support – to enhance coordinated efforts to build resilience against disinformation, including gendered disinformation.;;
