;MEX-24/0005;Strengthening voices: in defense of women's rights to communicate in MX ;MEX-1008;Human Rights in Mexico;B;2025;13.06.2025;Actual;206 671;0;NOK;2024;2026;Comunicación e Información de la Mujer A.C. CIMAC;Grant;4440;Mexico D.F.;0152;0152.70;0152.70.111;Menneskerettigheter;Mexico;U11974;Hammeren, Line;;03;;24.10.2024;CIMAC - Comunicacion e Informacion de la Mujer A.C.;CIMAC - Comunicacion e Informacion de la Mujer A.C.;NGO Local;I;Project- and programme grant;Bilateral;Project-type interventions;15160;151;Government and civil society, general;60;Human rights;;-;-;-;-;-;-;Main;Main;-;-;-;-;-;-;-;-;The Program of Liberty of Expression and Gender of CIMAC has been documenting and accompanying Mexican journalists for more than 19 years. CIMAC created the first network for female journalists in the country in 1993 and developed a feminist model for accompanying them. The project is focused on developing an integral and cross-cutting strategy that allocates women journalists rights in the center by developing legal strategies that will protect female journalists and strengthen their networks in the most violent states in Mexico.;;
;MEX-24/0005;Strengthening voices: in defense of women's rights to communicate in MX ;MEX-1008;Human Rights in Mexico;B;2025;28.11.2025;Planned;243 329;0;;2024;2026;;;4440;Mexico D.F.;0152;0152.70;0152.70.111;Menneskerettigheter;Mexico;U11974;Hammeren, Line;;03;;24.10.2024;CIMAC - Comunicacion e Informacion de la Mujer A.C.;CIMAC - Comunicacion e Informacion de la Mujer A.C.;NGO Local;I;Project- and programme grant;Bilateral;Project-type interventions;15160;151;Government and civil society, general;60;Human rights;;-;-;-;-;-;-;Main;Main;-;-;-;-;-;-;-;-;The Program of Liberty of Expression and Gender of CIMAC has been documenting and accompanying Mexican journalists for more than 19 years. CIMAC created the first network for female journalists in the country in 1993 and developed a feminist model for accompanying them. The project is focused on developing an integral and cross-cutting strategy that allocates women journalists rights in the center by developing legal strategies that will protect female journalists and strengthen their networks in the most violent states in Mexico.;;
;MEX-25/0002;Film Without Borders Festival;MEX-1006;Culture and Private Sector promotion ;B;2025;18.11.2025;Verified;10 000;0;NOK;2025;2025;Ana Lucía Rodríguez Alavéz;Grant;4440;Mexico D.F.;0115;0115.70;0115.70.112;Kultur- og informasjonsformål - ute/stasjonene;Mexico;U17947;Gonzalez Duncan, Viveka Alexandra;;02;;14.11.2025;Undefined (Ana Lucia Rodriguez Alavez);Undefined (Ana Lucia Rodriguez Alavez);NGO Local;III;Small-scale grant;Bilateral;Development awareness;99820;998;Unallocated/unspecified;20;Promotion of development awareness;;-;-;-;-;-;-;-;-;-;-;-;-;-;-;-;-;The Cine Sin Fronteras – Tijuana 2025 Festival (Film Withour Borders) is an international documentary film festival that includes panel discussions, master classes, and audiovisual training workshops focused on human rights, migration, and dignified mobility. It will take place at the Tijuana Cultural Center (CECUT) and other community venues, with the participation of filmmakers, activists, and social organizations from Latin America. A Meeting of Human Rights Film Festivals of Abya Yala will also be held, bringing together representatives from more than ten countries to strengthen the Latin American network for exhibition and cultural cooperation. It is a partnership between the Contra el Silencio Todas las Voces Festival (Mexico), the Colombia Migrante Film Festival (Colombia) and the International Human Rights Film Festival (Argentina). This initiative uses film as a tool to raise awareness about forced displacement, the diaspora, and dignified migration, and seeks to consolidate a cultural pact for human mobility.;;
