;MOZ-17/0001;Rights, Equality, SRHR & Adolescents in Mozambique;MOZ-3105;Support towards implementation on GBV, SRHR and LGTB-rights ;B;2025;10.06.2025;Actual;5 000 000;0;NOK;2017;2026;Pathfinder International Mozambique;Grant;4435;Maputo/Mozambique;0159;0159.75;0159.75.111;Afrika - nasjonale tiltak;Mozambique;U17178;Cuamba, Denise;201700076;03;;28.08.2017;Pathfinder International;Pathfinder International;NGO International;I;Project- and programme grant;Bilateral;Project-type interventions;13030;130;Population policies/programmes and reproductive health;30;Family planning;;-;-;-;-;-;-;Main;-;-;-;-;-;-;Main;-;-;The initiative aims to consolidate and expand on previous support initiative. The project will address inequitable gender norms to strengthen adolescents’ SRHR outcomes while improving the availability and accessibility of quality Gender Based Violence (GBV) primary and secondary prevention, Comprehensive Abortion Care (CAC), and SRHR services. The aim is to improve adolescent sexual reproductive health in Maputo, Gaza, Inhambane and Cabo Delgado provinces by increasing gender equality  ;;
;MOZ-17/0011;Energia para todos: A Multi-donor trust fund for electricity access;MOZ-3109;EDM transmission and distribution emergency invesments;B;2025;22.11.2025;Planned;30 000 000;0;;2018;2026;World bank;;4435;Maputo/Mozambique;0159;0159.75;0159.75.111;Afrika - nasjonale tiltak;Mozambique;U14815;Vikjord, Vemund;;03;;12.12.2018;IBRD - International Bank for Reconstruction and Development;IBRD - International Bank for Reconstruction and Development;International Monetary Fund (IMF), World Bank (WB) and World Trade Organisation (WTO);I;Project- and programme grant;Earmarked to multilaterals;Contributions to multi-donor/single-entity funding mechanisms;23630;236;Heating, cooling and energy distribution;30;Electric power transmission and distribution (centralised grids);;-;-;-;-;-;-;Significant;Significant;-;-;-;-;-;-;-;-;Support to increased access to electricity through a Multi Donor Trust Fund administered by the World Bank. The program is aligned with the new national electrification strategy aiming at universal access to electricity by 2030. Only about 30 percent of the population have access to electricity in Mozambique. Energy for all (Sustainable Development goal 7) is a priority for the Norwegian Government. The project has a strong gender equality component and plan to improve women's empowerment.;SDG7 – Access to affordable and clean energy in Mozambique depends on further strengthening and development of the national grid. Norway has pooled resources allocated to densification with Sweden

