;MWI-18/0014;Our Rights, Our Lives and Our Future: Comprehensive sexuality education;MWI-2676;Sexual and reporductive health and rights;C;2025;28.02.2025;Actual;- 1 314 721;0;NOK;2019;2023;UNESCO;Grant;4385;Lilongwe/Malawi;0159;0159.75;0159.75.111;Afrika - nasjonale tiltak;Malawi;U18395;Chaweza, Chisomo Godfrey;;03;;10.10.2019;UNESCO - UN Educational, Scientific and Cultural Organisation;UNESCO - UN Educational, Scientific and Cultural Organisation;United Nations;I;Project- and programme grant;Earmarked to multilaterals;Project-type interventions;11220;112;Basic education;20;Primary education;;-;-;-;-;-;-;Significant;Significant;-;-;-;-;-;Significant;-;Significant;This project will contribute to changes so that adolecent and young people in Malawi are empowered, educated, healty and resilient and have the capacity to reach their full potential through receiving good quality comprehensive sexuality education (CSE). The project aims at primary education and will focus on competence building for teachers, capasity building for government at all levels, curriculum and policy development and advocasy for CSE in Malawi.;To follow up global goals as well as the ambassys priorities in education in Malawi;
;MWI-19/0018;LUANAR - Sustainable Food Systems  in Malawi (FOODMA) Programme;MWI-2683;Agriculture, Food Security, Climate & Environment;B;2025;30.09.2025;Actual;3 800 000;0;NOK;2020;2026;NORWEGIAN UNIVERSITY OF LIFE SCIENCES;Grant;4385;Lilongwe/Malawi;0159;0159.75;0159.75.111;Afrika - nasjonale tiltak;Malawi;AUC;Chikuni, Augustine Charles;;03;;01.12.2020;Malawi Ministry of Finance;LUANAR - Lilongwe University of Agriculture and Natural Resources;Governments/Ministries in developing countries;I;Project- and programme grant;Bilateral;Project-type interventions;43071;430;Other multisector;71;Food security policy and administrative management;;-;-;-;-;-;Significant;-;-;-;Main;-;-;Main;-;-;-;The objectives of the FoodMa is to strengthen local food systems in selected Extension Planning Areas  in five districts of Malawi. Its goal is to contribute towards resilient sustainable food systems and it is expeced that the project will lead to improved food and nutrition security in addition to increasing income among the agriculture-dependent rural households in Malawi.;The objectives of the FoodMa is to strengthen local food systems in selected Extension Planning Areas  in five districts of Malawi. Its goal is to contribute towards resilient sustainable food systems and it is expeced that the project will lead to improved food and nutrition security in addition to increasing income among the agriculture-dependent rural households in Malawi.

;Gammel beskrivesle: Catalytic funding to support the Education Services Joint Fund. The government needs capacity building and technical assistance in the implementation of activities through the Education Services Joint Fund (ESJF). Support to the Technical Implementation Consultant and also to the Fiduciary agent is part of this agreement. Norways contribution to the ESJF needs for it to have the right implact to be supported by technical staff to help improve the capacity of government, at national, regional and local level to be able to improve the education system in Malawi. Agreement involves technical support to Malawi government on inclusive education, teacher contiuous professional development and evidence based policy development.;
