;MWI-22/0005;Adr contraceptives and SRHR for teenagers through trad and faith leaders;MWI-2676;Sexual and reporductive health and rights;B;2025;18.09.2025;Actual;1 764 289;0;NOK;2023;2026;Kirkens Nødhjelp;Grant;4385;Lilongwe/Malawi;0159;0159.75;0159.75.111;Afrika - nasjonale tiltak;Malawi;U18258;Chavunya, Mathews Hotstix;;03;;30.11.2023;Kirkens Nødhjelp;Kirkens Nødhjelp;NGO Norwegian;I;Project- and programme grant;Bilateral;Project-type interventions;13030;130;Population policies/programmes and reproductive health;30;Family planning;;-;-;-;-;-;-;Main;-;-;-;-;-;-;Main;-;-;Increased levels of action by faith and traditional leaders to strengthen Sexual and Reproductive Health and Rights (SRHR), with the aim to reduce teenage pregnancies and early marriages in Malawi.;;
;MWI-22/0009;Strengthening Human Rights for Vulnerable Populations in Malawi;MWI-2655;Democratic Governance;B;2025;10.11.2025;Planned;4 151 000;0;;2023;2028;UNDP Contribution´s Accounts;;4385;Lilongwe/Malawi;0152;0152.70;0152.70.111;Menneskerettigheter;Malawi;MINY;Nyirenda, Michael;;03;;04.12.2023;UNDP - UN Development Programme;UNDP - UN Development Programme;United Nations;I;Project- and programme grant;Earmarked to multilaterals;Project-type interventions;15160;151;Government and civil society, general;60;Human rights;;-;-;-;-;-;-;Main;Main;-;-;-;-;-;-;-;-;The Embassy will explore support to key human rights institutions such as the Office of Ombudsman and Human Rights Commission to enhance their capacity to promote and protect rights of Malawians, and support their complementary roles to UN agencies  including the Resident Coordinator and UNDP.;Human rights institutions in Malawi play and increasing important role in ensuring the promotion and protection of rights by all citizens including minorities and disadvantaged groups. they also have been critical for facilittaiting and promoting accountability for rights denied and or vilolated. The Office of the Ombudsman has increased risen to the occassion in this respect with determinations that the equaivalent force of a court of law. The human Rights Commission has also been central to highlighting and investigaging rights abuses. Civil society actors such as the Public Affairs Committee have been central in pushing for political action an accountability for upholding of rights by political players and officers. Support to these institutions has been declining in recent years, despite their essentail complementary roles to the work of UN agencies focusing on promotion and protection of human rights.;
;MWI-23/0001;O3: Comprehensive Sexuality Education in Malawi Phase II;MWI-2676;Sexual and reporductive health and rights;B;2025;30.10.2025;Planned;10 000 000;0;;2024;2027;UNESCO;;4385;Lilongwe/Malawi;0159;0159.75;0159.75.111;Afrika - nasjonale tiltak;Malawi;U18395;Chaweza, Chisomo Godfrey;;03;;27.09.2024;UNESCO - UN Educational, Scientific and Cultural Organisation;UNESCO - UN Educational, Scientific and Cultural Organisation;United Nations;I;Project- and programme grant;Earmarked to multilaterals;Project-type interventions;12261;122;Basic health;61;Health education;;-;-;-;-;-;-;Main;-;-;-;-;-;-;Main;-;Significant;This project is designed to deliver good quality CSE that empowers adolescents and young people in Malawi and builds agency while developing the skills, knowledge, attitudes and competencies required for preventing HIV, reducing early and unintended pregnancies, and eliminating gender-based violence. This project seeks to build on young people’s individual capacity of making safer choices while strengthening the linkages between information (CSE) and sexual and reproductive health services provision. As a follow-on from Phase I (MWI-18/0014), the project aims to continue the work on CSE targeting primary education, and will focus on competency building for teachers, capacity building for government at all levels, continued support towards the finalisation of the Life Skills curriculum  and its implementation, policy development and advocacy for CSE in Malawi. ;To follow up global goals as well as Norwegian priorities on SRHR and CSE.;
