;MWI-24/0010;Frontier Investment Feasibility renewable energy projects Malawi;QZA-0996;Private sector and de-risking;B;2025;04.12.2025;Planned;8 555 850;0;;2024;2027;Frontier Investment Management ApS;;300513;KNN-ENERGI Seksjon for energi;0162;0162.72;0162.72.122;Bedriftsstøtte - fornybar energi;Malawi;NORAD-U12655;Berg, Jannike;2400820;03;;11.12.2024;Nyika Hydropower Group Ltd.;Nyika Hydropower Group Ltd.;Private sector in developing countries;I;Project- and programme grant;Bilateral;Project-type interventions;23210;232;Energy generation, renewable sources;10;Energy generation, renewable sources – multiple technologies;;-;-;-;-;-;Main;-;-;-;-;-;Significant;-;-;-;-;Frontier Investment Management ApS har applied for and been approved NOK 10 million in support for feasibility studies of 50 MW wind and 51 MW run of river hydropower projects in Malawi. The Grant Agreement is entered into between Norad and NyikaHydropower Group Limited, a wholly owned subsidiary of Frontier Energy, the investment fund managed by Frontier Investment Management ApS. Nyika Hydorpower Group Ltd is the spesial purpose vehicle (SPV) for the hydropower project Frontier is developing in Malawi. The wind project is developed by another SPV owned by Frontier and will be a sub-grantee under the Grant Agreement.;;
