;MWI-24/0013;Malawi Accountability and Transparency Support;MWI-2655;Democratic Governance;A;2025;01.11.2025;Planned;2 500 000;0;;2025;2028;;;4385;Lilongwe/Malawi;0159;0159.75;0159.75.111;Afrika - nasjonale tiltak;Malawi;MINY;Nyirenda, Michael;;03;;;FCDO - Foreign, Commonwealth and Development Office (UK);;Public sector other donor countries;I;Project- and programme grant;Bilateral;Project-type interventions;15113;151;Government and civil society, general;13;Anti-corruption organisations and institutions ;;-;-;-;-;-;-;-;Main;-;-;-;-;-;-;-;-;The embassy will support accountability and transparency initiatives that  improve and sustain democratic gains especially  anti-corruption initailly by collaborating with FCDO. Tackling Serious Oragnized Crime (TSOC) aims to strengthen the anti-corruption environment and increase the likelihood and severity of sanctions for serious and organised corruption and related crimes in Malawi.  Civil society actors and the media have been central in pushing for political action an accountability and public sector reform in Malawi.  Support to these institutions has been declining in recent years, despite their key roles in sustaining democratic values. ;;
;MWI-24/0014;Strengthenening the rights of minorities in Malawi;MWI-2655;Democratic Governance;A;2025;02.06.2025;Planned;1 500 000;0;;2025;2028;;;4385;Lilongwe/Malawi;0152;0152.70;0152.70.111;Menneskerettigheter;Malawi;U18172;Hauger, Rune;;03;;;;;;I;Project- and programme grant;;;00000;000;Sector not planned ;00;Sector not planned;;-;-;-;-;-;-;-;-;-;-;-;-;-;-;-;-;The project will build on the sucesses and lessons of project MWI-19/0003 and previous efforts in the area of strengthening minority rights in Malawi. The Embassy is currently exploring ways to strenghten the rights-based approach, looking into possibilities of supporting representative LGBTI+ organisations in addition to the CSOs that we have previously supported.;;
