;PAK-21/0008;Youth Empowerment on SRHR (YES!) Advancing the Sexual and Reproductive Health and Rights of Young People in Sindh and Punjab;PAK-3017;Womens Grant;C;2025;30.06.2025;Actual;558 000;0;NOK;2022;2025;AAHUNG-IWHC-PHASE-4;Grant;4320;Islamabad/Pakistan;0159;0159.76;0159.76.111;Asia - nasjonale tiltak;Pakistan;U15194;Myrtveit, Anja Benedicte;23/6026;03;;05.12.2022;Aahung;Aahung;NGO Local;I;Project- and programme grant;Bilateral;Project-type interventions;13030;130;Population policies/programmes and reproductive health;30;Family planning;;-;-;-;-;-;-;Main;-;-;-;-;-;-;Main;-;-;The overall objective of this project is to improve sexual and reproductive health outcomes of young people in Pakistan by increasing access to information and services, and decreasing associated stigma. The program will target young people, particularly girls, 12 years and above through school based interventions, young people between 16 and 24 years at the community level, young people 16 and above through digital and other communications platforms, medical and nursing students who are most commonly 18-22 years, and policy makers/decision makers who are relevant to enacting policy change and developing public programs that impact the SRHR of young people.   ;;
;PAK-21/0010;Building long-term resilience of flood-affected communities - Food security Interventions in Sindh Province;PAK-3061;Climate Pakistan;B;2025;01.12.2025;Planned;10 000 000;0;;2022;2026;WFP London Donation Acc. USD;;4320;Islamabad/Pakistan;0159;0159.76;0159.76.111;Asia - nasjonale tiltak;Pakistan;U16926;Majeed, Bilal Mohammad;23/6037;03;;06.12.2022;WFP - World Food Programme;WFP - World Food Programme;United Nations;I;Project- and programme grant;Earmarked to multilaterals;Contributions to multi-donor/single-entity funding mechanisms;43072;430;Other multisector;72;Household food security programmes ;;-;-;-;-;-;-;-;-;-;-;-;-;Significant;-;Main;-;The overall goals of the project are to address both, a) the immediate life-saving food and other essential needs of flood-affected households, and b) to provide longer-term support to disaster-prone communities, in districts of Sindh province, enabling them to enhance their resilience to future climatic risks and environmental degradation. This approach aims to improve food security and establish sustainable livelihoods. In its first year, the project will target communities of district Ghotki and Badin, primarily focusing on achieving the immediate food needs of the most vulnerable flood-affected households through unconditional cash assistance. In the subsequent three years, the project will strive to enhance the drought resilience of vulnerable households & small-scale farmers of district Qambar Shahdat Kot & Jacobabad, by providing training and creating relevant community assets, thereby diversifying livelihoods, and increasing crop and livestock production.;STAT: Bistandsform B032 da det er multidonor

