S;QZA-21/0162-16;NORHED II iCARTA;QZA-0945;NORHED II;B;2025;12.03.2025;Actual;342 665;0;NOK;2021;2026;Universitetet i Bergen;Grant;300523;VEM-UTFORSK Seksjon for utdanning og forskning;0161;0161.70;0161.70.139;NORHED II;Kenya;NORAD-U18076;Rand, Tor-Øyvind;;03;;07.05.2021;UiB - Universitetet i Bergen;APHRC - African Population and Health Research Center;Norwegian public sector;I(S);Project- and programme grant - with subunits;Triangular co-operation;Other technical assistance;11420;114;Post-secondary education;20;Higher education;;-;-;-;-;-;-;Significant;-;-;Main;-;-;-;-;-;-;I-CARTA will set up mechanisms to institutionalise a set of previously tested interventions to improve the quality of research training and research to improve pubic and population health in Africa. The project seeks to produce high-quality early career researchers (ECRs) who grow into research leaders and enhance engagement between the CARTA community (ERC’s, supervisors, graduates) and society to influence policy and programmatic change to improve long-term health outcomes.;;
