;QZA-21/0280;Hfu - IMO TEST Biofouling;QZA-0896;Hfu - Oceans for Development;B;2025;19.11.2025;Verified;11 786 336;0;NOK;2021;2026;IMO DONOR FUNDS 2100 USD;Grant;300514;KNN-HAV Seksjon for hav;0163;0163.71;0163.71.123;Hav for utvikling;Global Unspecified;NORAD-U16499;Johansen, Kari Synnøve;2100535;03;;07.12.2021;IMO - International Maritime Organisation;IMO - International Maritime Organisation;United Nations;I;Project- and programme grant;Earmarked to multilaterals;Contributions to single-donor funding mechanisms and contributions earmarked for a specific funding window or geographical locat;41010;410;General environmental protection;10;Environmental policy and administrative management;Kunnskapsbanken;-;-;-;-;-;Main;Significant;-;Significant;-;-;Significant;-;-;-;-;The “Accelerating Transfer of Environmentally sound Technologies through demonstration pilots to reduce biofouling and related emissions” (TEST Biofouling). Project will assist developing countries to build their knowledge on control and management of biofouling and showcase effective approaches to biofouling management and the mitigation of environmental risks associated with the transfer of Invasive Aquatic Species (IAS) through biofouling by means of demonstration projects at both regional and country level. Invasive aquatic species (IAS) is a major threat to marine and coastal biodiversity. Improving biofouling management can also enhance ships’ energy efficiency and reduce greenhouse gas emissions from ships. The project also includes a Gender Action Plan with three key objectives: 1: Gender equality as a business case in the maritime sector. 2: Qualitative gender data gathered and analyzed. 3: Monitoring and delivery of IMO project-specific gender related activities.

;Addendum nr 1: no cost extension until 31 Dcember 2026 (2100535-45);
