;QZA-21/0283;NIVA Substantive and Equal participation for a legally binding Plastic Treaty;QZA-0927;Climate and environment;B;2025;22.08.2025;Actual;5 382 944;0;NOK;2022;2025;Norsk Institutt for vannforskning;Grant;300514;KNN-HAV Seksjon for hav;0163;0163.71;0163.71.122;Marin forsøpling program;Global Unspecified;NORAD-U18904;Andresen, Per Magnus;2201651;03;;06.12.2022;NIVA - Norsk institutt for vannforskning;NIVA - Norsk institutt for vannforskning;NGO Norwegian;I;Project- and programme grant;Bilateral;Project-type interventions;14050;140;Water and sanitation;50;Waste management/disposal;;-;-;-;-;-;Main;-;-;-;-;-;-;-;-;-;-;The project is co-developed by NIVA, CIEL, CEJAD and EIA. It will ensure substantive and equal participation of government officials and civil society actors from developing countries and economies in transition throughout the negotiations for an international legally binding instrument to end plastic pollution. The geographical focus will be on three regions (the Pacific, Africa and Asia) and the proposed target groups are state delegates participating in the INC process and civil society actors (CSAs). Within these three regions, the project will target specific country champions - Rwanda, Senegal, Indonesia, Viet Nam, Samoa and the Federated States of Micronesia (FSM).;;
;QZA-21/0293;Students at risk (StAR) 2022-2025;GLO-4024;Human Rights defenders;B;2025;26.11.2025;Planned;13 800 000;0;;2022;2025;Direktoratet for høyere utdanning og kompetanse;;470201;Seksjon for menneskerettigheter, partnerskap og ny teknologi;0152;0152.70;0152.70.111;Menneskerettigheter;Global Unspecified;ANEN;Enersen, Anniken;21/4060;03;;24.05.2022;HK-dir - Direktoratet for høyere utdanning og kompetanse;HK-dir - Direktoratet for høyere utdanning og kompetanse;Norwegian public sector;V;Delegation to governmental grant manager;Bilateral;Project-type interventions;11420;114;Post-secondary education;20;Higher education;;-;-;-;-;-;-;Significant;Main;-;-;-;-;-;-;-;-;Support to Students at Risk (StAR), which is a programme that gives students, who have experienced persecution, threats or expulsion from their higher education institution because of their peaceful activism and fight for human rights and democratic change, a chance to finish their education abroad. The programme aims to achieve gender balance in nominations and intake of students.;Only available for students from OECD-DAC countries.;
