S;QZA-21/0324-1;Just Leaders: Leadership for Social Justice in Higher Education;QZA-0970;Inclusion in higher education;B;2025;18.03.2025;Actual;1 431 891;0;NOK;2022;2026;SAIH;Grant;300523;VEM-UTFORSK Seksjon for utdanning og forskning;0170;0170.70;0170.70.121;Bistandsavtaler norske organisasjoner;South Africa;NORAD-U18076;Rand, Tor-Øyvind;2100653;03;;08.04.2022;SAIH - Studentenes og Akademikernes Internasjonale Hjelpefond;University of Pretoria;NGO Norwegian;I(S);Project- and programme grant - with subunits;Bilateral;Core support to NGOs, other private bodies, PPPs and research institutes;11420;114;Post-secondary education;20;Higher education;;-;-;-;-;-;-;Main;Main;-;-;-;-;-;Significant;-;Significant;The Centre for Sexualities Aids and Gender identity at the University of Pretoria collaborate with five other univerisities in the region on student leadership and awareness of LGBTIQA+ issues. Strenghten student bodies, research and influencing policies for inclusive higher education. At the core of SAIHs work are the SDGs and the principle of leaving no-one behind. The programme focuses on groups that have historically been oppressed because they are indigenous, afro-descendants or other ethnic minorities, women, LGBTQIA+, live with disabilities, or come from lower socioeconomic backgrounds. ;;
