;QZA-22/0084;Legacy Landscapes Fund;QZA-0982;Climate services;B;2025;24.10.2025;Actual;25 000 000;0;NOK;2022;2026;Internationaler Naturerbe Fonds - Legacy Lanscapes Fund;Grant;300516;KNN-NAKLI Seksjon for natur og klima;0163;0163.70;0163.70.131;Miljø og klima;Global Unspecified;NORAD-U17576;Syversen, Hanne Grimsrud;2201273;03;;08.12.2022;LLF - Legacy Landscapes Fund;LLF - Legacy Landscapes Fund;NGO Other donor countries;II;General funding grant;Bilateral;Contributions to specific-purpose programmes and funds managed by implementing partners;41030;410;General environmental protection;30;Bio-diversity;;-;-;-;-;-;Main;-;Significant;Main;-;-;Significant;Significant;-;-;-;This agreement will support the Legacy Landscapes Fund in protecting natural places, preserve the ecological functions of the protected areas as well as their buffer zones, and closing the funding gap for biodiversity conservation in the Global South. Effectively managed conservation areas are seen as one of the most important instruments for preserving biodiversity, contribute to climate adaptation and mitigation and to reducing the risk of zoonoses. Grantees of the foundation are NGOs in partnership with national conservation authorities/custodians of land as well as indigenous and local communities. The foundation brings together public and private contributions.;;
