;QZA-22/0214;CEPI: Softly earmarked support to Coalition for Epidemic Preparedness Innovation (2022-2026);NOR-0037;CEPI Sekretariat;B;2025;19.05.2025;Actual;200 000 000;0;NOK;2022;2026;IBRD;Grant;300522;VEM-HELSE Seksjon for helse;0160;0160.70;0160.70.152;Forskning, produktutvikling og innovasjon;Global Unspecified;NORAD-AUDA;Davis, Austen Peter;2201866;03;;15.12.2022;CEPI - Coalition for Epidemic Preparedness Innovations;CEPI - Coalition for Epidemic Preparedness Innovations;Public-private partnerships;I;Project- and programme grant;Bilateral;Contributions to multi-donor/single-entity funding mechanisms;12250;122;Basic health;50;Infectious disease control;;-;1;-;-;-;-;-;-;-;Main;-;-;-;-;-;-;Softly earmarked support to CEPI 2.0 to activity portfolios identified as Official Development Assistance (ODA).  CEPI is a partnership of public, private and humanitarian org. During the first strategy period 2017-2021 (CEPI 1.0), the Coalition has funded the development of vaccines against selected diseases with potential for becoming major epidemics. Amid CEPI 1,0, the covid-19 pandemic struck, and CEPI played a major role in the global response as lead for the vaccine R&D. In its new strategy period 2022-2026, CEPI will continue its work on core pathogens, the development of broadly protective coronavirus vaccine, and will still support the development and testing of new platform technologies so that new vaccines can quickly be developed when unknown pathogens strike.;;
