;QZA-23/0108;AMPLIFY CHANGE Core Contribution 2023-2027;QZA-0199;Sexual and Reproductive Health and Rights;B;2025;19.05.2025;Actual;7 500 000;0;NOK;2023;2027;AmplifyChange;Grant;300524;VEM-LIKE Seksjon for likestilling;0170;0170.70;0170.70.122;Internasjonale organisasjoner og nettverk;Global Unspecified;NORAD-CHSA;Salvesen, Camilla Holst;2202270;03;;09.06.2023;AC - AmplifyChange;AC - AmplifyChange;NGO International;II;General funding grant;Bilateral;Core support to NGOs, other private bodies, PPPs and research institutes;13030;130;Population policies/programmes and reproductive health;30;Family planning;;-;-;-;-;-;-;Main;-;-;-;-;-;-;Main;-;Significant;Agreement title: Ensuring healthy lives: Local organisations’ leadership on CSE and SRHR. Amplify Change is multi-donor fund supporting grassroot civil society organisations advocating for improved SRHR on different levels. The subgrants span the spectrum of SRHR such as CSE, abortion and access to reproductive health care, including family planning. AmplifyChange has a strong focus on women and youth in all their diversities, with a priority to marginalized and vulnerable groups including people living with disabilities, with HIV/AIDS, and in conflict-affected areas.;;
