;QZA-23/0142;Support to Front Line Defenders 2023-2026;GLO-4024;Human Rights defenders;B;2025;07.07.2025;Actual;3 000 000;0;NOK;2023;2026;Front Line;Grant;300525;VEM-MRS Seksjon for mennesterettigheter og sivilt samfunn;0152;0152.70;0152.70.111;Menneskerettigheter;Global Unspecified;NORAD-U18367;Tordhol, Tor Håkon;2400617;03;;28.11.2023;Front Line Defenders;Front Line Defenders;NGO International;II;General funding grant;Bilateral;Core support to NGOs, other private bodies, PPPs and research institutes;15160;151;Government and civil society, general;60;Human rights;;-;-;-;-;-;-;Significant;Main;-;-;-;-;-;-;-;-;Support to the implementation of Front Line Defenders (FLD) Strategic Plan for 2023-2027 in the period 2023-2026. Front Line Defender's programme aims to ensure that: human rights defenders are reognised and supported as essential actors in defending and advancing human rights, and bringing about positive change in society. FLD will contribute to this by providing increased protection through the provision of rapid, practical and intersectional support to HRDs, ensure that HRDs, their communities and civil society have strengthened resilience and capacity to manage their protection in the longer-term, and work for stronger policies and political/practical action at national, regional and international levels to protect human rights defenders at risk. The main target group is human rights defenders, including women human rights defenders, and human rights organisations at risk in developing countries, supporting them to safely continue their essential work to promote human rights in their communities.;;
