;QZA-23/0143;IMF Global Public Finance Partnership - GPFP;QZA-0792;Tax for Development Phase 2;B;2025;07.05.2025;Actual;25 000 000;0;NOK;2025;2027;International Monetary Fund;Grant;300526;VEM-STYRE Seksjon for styresett;0161;0161.73;0161.73.114;Skatt for utvikling;Global Unspecified;NORAD-U1294;Bakke, Alf Rasmus;2500042;03;;31.03.2025;IMF - International Monetary Fund;IMF - International Monetary Fund;International Monetary Fund (IMF), World Bank (WB) and World Trade Organisation (WTO);I;Project- and programme grant;Earmarked to multilaterals;Contributions to multi-donor/single-entity funding mechanisms;15114;151;Government and civil society, general;14;Domestic Revenue Mobilisation;Kunnskapsbanken;-;-;-;-;-;-;-;Main;-;-;-;-;-;-;-;-;The Revenue and Public Finance - initiative will promote revenue mobilization and capacity development of public finance systems  in support of sustainable development. It will provide technical assistance for a select group of countries and global knowledge to achieve this. The expected outcomes are enhanced revenue outcomes and better use of public finance in partner countries. This is a new Umbrella trust fund that merges current revenue trust funds (RMTF and TADAT) and revenues from natural rescources (MNRW) and IMF programs on public expenditure and public finance management. The Revenue areas will be the main area and will cover around 2/3 of the TF. Totally 60 countries supported, among them Malawi, Mozambique and Tanzania.;;
