;RAF-21/0036;The Social Sciences in an Era of transitions and transformation;RAF-3058;Research cooperation with institutions in sub-Saharan Africa;B;2025;23.09.2025;Actual;11 000 000;0;NOK;2022;2027;CC USD CODESRIA;Grant;300523;VEM-UTFORSK Seksjon for utdanning og forskning;0161;0161.71;0161.71.113;Kapasitetsbygging innenfor forskning og høyere utdanning;Africa Regional;NORAD-U16709;Benjaminsen, Grete;;03;;28.11.2022;CODESRIA - Council for the Development of Economic Social Science Research in Africa;CODESRIA - Council for the Development of Economic Social Science Research in Africa;NGO International;I;Project- and programme grant;Bilateral;Core support to NGOs, other private bodies, PPPs and research institutes;43082;430;Other multisector;82;Research/scientific institutions;;-;-;-;-;-;Significant;Significant;Significant;-;Main;-;-;Significant;-;-;-;Core support to CODESRIA and its strategic plan (2022-2023), which overall goal is to increase the contributions of Africans to the task of understanding, interpreting and addressing key challenges facing the African continent. The thematic priorities are 1) The state and democratization in Africa 2) Economies and Economic Policy in Africa 3) Ecologies and Society in Africa (including issues related to the environment and climate change) and 4) Higher Education Dynamics in Africa. Gender is a cross-cutting issue. CODESRIA offers African scholars (with a specific focus on female researchers) network, research training, funding and possibilities for publishing their work. There are specific budget lines for scholarships and research grants to female researchers, and gender research schools are organized on a regular basis – to which African researchers are invited to present and discuss research on various topics related to gender and gender equality i Africa.;;
;RAF-21/0037;Strengthening the roles of science granting councils in Africa's science systems;RAF-3058;Research cooperation with institutions in sub-Saharan Africa;B;2025;26.08.2025;Actual;14 086 300;0;NOK;2022;2025;IDRC;Grant;300523;VEM-UTFORSK Seksjon for utdanning og forskning;0161;0161.71;0161.71.113;Kapasitetsbygging innenfor forskning og høyere utdanning;South of Sahara Regional;NORAD-U14294;Thorkildsen, Kjersti;2100769;03;;13.12.2021;IDRC - Canada's International Development Research Centre;IDRC - Canada's International Development Research Centre;Public sector other donor countries;I;Project- and programme grant;Bilateral;Project-type interventions;43082;430;Other multisector;82;Research/scientific institutions;;-;-;-;-;-;-;Significant;-;-;Main;-;-;-;-;-;-;The Programme titled “Strengthening the roles of science granting councils in Africa’s science systems“ is part of the Science Granting Councils Initiative phase 2 (SGCI-2) funded by IDRC

