;RAF-22/0028;NMU: Fishforce Phase II - Addressing Fisheries Crime Through Training, Research and Cooperation;RSA-3133;Support to the blue economy;B;2025;10.04.2025;Actual;2 024 258;0;NOK;2023;2026;Nelson Mandela University;Procurement;4545;Pretoria;0159;0159.75;0159.75.111;Afrika - nasjonale tiltak;South of Sahara Regional;BEM;Mokgoro, Kegomoditswe;;03;;18.07.2023;Nelson Mandela Metropolitan University;Nelson Mandela Metropolitan University;Public sector in developing countries;I;Project- and programme grant;Bilateral;Other technical assistance;31320;313;Fishing;20;Fishery development;;-;-;-;-;-;Main;-;-;Significant;Main;-;-;-;-;-;-;The FishFORCE project aims for Southern African countries to collaborate in cross border knowledge- and intelligence-led fisheries law enforcement to reduce illegal fishing and fisheries crimes in the region. Governments and intergovernmental organisations strengthen their fisheries and ocean policy frameworks for compliance and law enforcement. Involving SADC region countries including Kenya, Mauritius, Mozambique, Namibia, Tanzania and South Africa.;;
