;RAF-22/0029;African Fertilizer Financing Mechanism_African Emergency Food Production Facility;QZA-0803;Food security and Nutrition;C;2025;24.06.2025;Actual;8 000 000;0;NOK;2022;2032;African Development Bank/Africa Fertilizer Financing Mechanism (AFDB/AFFM);Grant;300512;KNN-MAT Seksjon for mat;0162;0162.71;0162.71.111;Matsikkerhet, fisk og landbruk;Africa Regional;NORAD-U13432;Langhus, Åsta Ingvild;;03;;13.12.2022;AFDB - African Development Bank;AFAP - African Fertilizer and Agribusiness Partnership;Regional Development Banks;I;Project- and programme grant;Earmarked to multilaterals;Contributions to multi-donor/single-entity funding mechanisms;31150;311;Agriculture;50;Agricultural inputs;;-;-;-;-;-;-;-;-;-;-;-;-;-;-;-;-;The African Union has established the African Fertilizer Financing Mechanism (AFFM) under the African Development Bank (AfDB) through the Abuja Declaration on Fertilizer for the African Green Revolution. As a response to the 2022 food crisis AfDB has applied for funds to AFFM under its African Emergency Food Production Facility (AEFPF). Under the AFFM credit guarantees will be offered to fertilizer suppliers

