S;RAF-23/0048-2;Growing together Tanzania program;RAF-3101;Civil Society Food Security;B;2025;13.10.2025;Planned;17 454 545;0;;2024;2028;IDH Sustainable Trade Initiative;;300512;KNN-MAT Seksjon for mat;0162;0162.71;0162.71.111;Matsikkerhet, fisk og landbruk;Tanzania;NORAD-U16160;Melby, Maria;2301554;03;;12.12.2023;IDH - The Sustainable Trade Initiative;IDH - The Sustainable Trade Initiative;NGO International;I(S);Project- and programme grant - with subunits;Bilateral;Project-type interventions;31110;311;Agriculture;10;Agricultural policy and administrative management;;-;-;-;-;-;Main;Significant;-;-;Significant;-;-;Significant;-;-;-;The 'Growing Together' program is a partnership between IDH, civil society groups (EAGC and Rikolto), and research bodies (CIAT). The program will collaborate with governments, major food enterprises, and SMEs with the aim to restructure food markets, enhance security, and uplift farmers. The initiative's goal is to bolster healthy food production, while reducing vulnerabilities to impacts from climate change in food producing landscapes by applying climate resilient farming practices and improving value chains in Tanzania with a focus om women’s participation.;;
