;RAF-25/0021;Health, Empowerment, and Rights (HER) Future Project;TAN-3174;TAN - Human Rights activities;A;2025;01.12.2025;Planned;15 000 000;0;;2025;2028;;;4230;Dar es Salaam/Tanzania;0159;0159.75;0159.75.111;Afrika - nasjonale tiltak;Africa Regional;U13144;Pettersen, Anette Otilie;202500099;03;;;Pathfinder International;Pathfinder International;NGO International;I;Project- and programme grant;Bilateral;Project-type interventions;15180;151;Government and civil society, general;80;Ending violence against women and girls;;-;-;-;-;-;-;Main;Significant;-;-;-;-;-;Significant;-;-;HER Future Project: A three-year initiative in Morogoro and Arusha regions (Tanzania), led by Pathfinder International and partners. It aims to ensure equitable access to sexual and reproductive health and rights (SRHR) for women, youth, and persons with disabilities by improving quality SRHR services, expanding age-appropriate comprehensive sexuality education, and fostering social and policy acceptance of sexual rights.;;
