;RAF-25/0041;Strengthening Democratic Resilience & Human Rights Through Media in NGA;RAF-3116;Norwegian Support to Civil Cociety Organisations in Nigeria 2025;B;2025;30.07.2025;Actual;1 500 000;0;NOK;2025;2027;Centre for Journalism Innovation and Development (CJID);Grant;4380;Abuja/Nigeria;0159;0159.75;0159.75.111;Afrika - nasjonale tiltak;Nigeria;U16600;Sidney, Chituru Stella;;03;;22.07.2025;CJID - Centre for Journalism Innovation and Development;CJID - Centre for Journalism Innovation and Development;NGO Local;I;Project- and programme grant;Bilateral;Contributions to specific-purpose programmes and funds managed by implementing partners;15153;151;Government and civil society, general;53;Media and free flow of information;;-;-;-;-;-;-;-;Main;-;-;-;-;-;-;-;-;This project will fortify democratic resilience and human rights protection in Nigeria by enhancing electoral integrity, accountability journalism, press freedom and citizen access to reliable information, especially during elctions and in conflict-affected areas. Focusing on selected states with national reach, the project will empower independent media to produce public-interest reporting that drives transparency and  civic participation. Special emphasis will be placed on Plateau and Benue states - hotspots for conflict and identity-based violence - where local journalists will receive training and mentorship to document failures and rights abuses through human-centered story telling.;;
;RAF-25/0041;Strengthening Democratic Resilience & Human Rights Through Media in NGA;RAF-3116;Norwegian Support to Civil Cociety Organisations in Nigeria 2025;B;2025;17.11.2025;Planned;1 500 000;0;;2025;2027;Centre for Journalism Innovation and Development (CJID);;4380;Abuja/Nigeria;0159;0159.75;0159.75.111;Afrika - nasjonale tiltak;Nigeria;U16600;Sidney, Chituru Stella;;03;;22.07.2025;CJID - Centre for Journalism Innovation and Development;CJID - Centre for Journalism Innovation and Development;NGO Local;I;Project- and programme grant;Bilateral;Contributions to specific-purpose programmes and funds managed by implementing partners;15153;151;Government and civil society, general;53;Media and free flow of information;;-;-;-;-;-;-;-;Main;-;-;-;-;-;-;-;-;This project will fortify democratic resilience and human rights protection in Nigeria by enhancing electoral integrity, accountability journalism, press freedom and citizen access to reliable information, especially during elctions and in conflict-affected areas. Focusing on selected states with national reach, the project will empower independent media to produce public-interest reporting that drives transparency and  civic participation. Special emphasis will be placed on Plateau and Benue states - hotspots for conflict and identity-based violence - where local journalists will receive training and mentorship to document failures and rights abuses through human-centered story telling.;;
;RAF-25/0042;Voix du Sahel ;RAF-3117;Democracy and governance in the Sahel;B;2025;13.11.2025;Actual;2 500 000;0;NOK;2025;2026;Fondation Hirondelle;Grant;4225;Dakar;0159;0159.75;0159.75.111;Afrika - nasjonale tiltak;Africa Regional;U15680;Kleiberg-Jensen, Camilla;;03;;07.11.2025;Hirondelle Foundation;Hirondelle Foundation;NGO International;I;Project- and programme grant;Bilateral;Project-type interventions;15153;151;Government and civil society, general;53;Media and free flow of information;;-;-;-;-;-;-;-;-;-;-;-;-;-;-;-;-;The overall goal or impact of the project Voix du Sahel – informer pour la paix et l’engagement citoyen (“Voice of the Sahel – informing for peace and civic engagement”) is to contribute to peace consolidation and the emergence of a democratic public space, through the promotion of reliable, independent, inclusive, and citizen-oriented information. The Project seeks to strengthen social cohesion and democratic dialogue at national and regional/local levels, while enhancing community resilience against disinformation and manipulation. It will emphasize the role of media as a driver of peacebuilding, civic participation, and inclusive governance. The project is implemented in Mali, Niger and Burkina Faso. ;;
