S;RER-23/0010-1;UNICEF Ukraine Response;QZA-1033;The Nansen Support Programme for Ukraine - HUM - international partners;B;2025;17.06.2025;Actual;210 000 000;0;NOK;2022;2026;UNICEF;Grant;300540;UKR-NANSEN Avdeling for Nansen-programmet for Ukraina;0159;0159.73;0159.73.112;Humanitær bistand;Ukraine;NORAD-U18919;Dibb, Rebecca Volckmar;2301989;03;;13.11.2023;UNICEF - United Nations Children's Fund;UNICEF - United Nations Children's Fund;United Nations;I(S);Project- and programme grant - with subunits;Earmarked to multilaterals;Contributions to multi-donor/single-entity funding mechanisms;72010;720;Emergency Response;10;Material relief assistance and services;;-;-;-;-;-;-;Significant;-;-;-;-;-;-;-;Main;-;Humanitarian funding to UNICEFs Humanitarian Action for CHildren (HAC) in Ukraine. UNICEF will sustain and expand its flexible, adaptive response to the unpredictable situation, including protection assistance, life-saving supplies, essential services, enhancement of social service capacities, preparedness for additional displacements and support to government systems. 5.3 million women and children accessing health care is one of the key planned targets of UNICEF’s Ukraine and refugee response.;;
S;RER-23/0010-1;UNICEF Ukraine Response;QZA-1033;The Nansen Support Programme for Ukraine - HUM - international partners;B;2025;21.10.2025;Planned;15 000 000;0;;2022;2026;UNICEF;;300540;UKR-NANSEN Avdeling for Nansen-programmet for Ukraina;0159;0159.73;0159.73.112;Humanitær bistand;Ukraine;NORAD-TAKV;Kvalvaag, Tale;2301989;03;;13.11.2023;UNICEF - United Nations Children's Fund;UNICEF - United Nations Children's Fund;United Nations;I(S);Project- and programme grant - with subunits;Earmarked to multilaterals;Contributions to multi-donor/single-entity funding mechanisms;72010;720;Emergency Response;10;Material relief assistance and services;;-;-;-;-;-;-;Significant;-;-;-;-;-;-;-;Main;-;Humanitarian funding to UNICEFs Humanitarian Action for CHildren (HAC) in Ukraine. UNICEF will sustain and expand its flexible, adaptive response to the unpredictable situation, including protection assistance, life-saving supplies, essential services, enhancement of social service capacities, preparedness for additional displacements and support to government systems. 5.3 million women and children accessing health care is one of the key planned targets of UNICEF’s Ukraine and refugee response.;;
S;RER-23/0010-2;UNICEF Regional Refugee Response;QZA-1033;The Nansen Support Programme for Ukraine - HUM - international partners;B;2025;17.06.2025;Actual;10 000 000;0;NOK;2022;2026;UNICEF;Grant;300540;UKR-NANSEN Avdeling for Nansen-programmet for Ukraina;0159;0159.73;0159.73.112;Humanitær bistand;Moldova;NORAD-U18919;Dibb, Rebecca Volckmar;2301989;03;;13.11.2023;UNICEF - United Nations Children's Fund;UNICEF - United Nations Children's Fund;United Nations;I(S);Project- and programme grant - with subunits;Earmarked to multilaterals;Contributions to multi-donor/single-entity funding mechanisms;72010;720;Emergency Response;10;Material relief assistance and services;;-;-;-;-;1;-;Significant;-;-;-;-;-;-;-;-;Significant;Implementation of UNICEF's Humanitarian Action for Children (HAC) for Ukraine and Refugee Response. UNICEF will sustain and expand its collaboration with national and local governrments to provide education, early learning, health, nutrition, child protection and social support for refugee families and children in Moldova. Cross-sectoral approaches in gender, adolescent development, and disability will be incorporated.;;
S;RER-23/0010-3;UNICEF reintegration of children;QZA-1033;The Nansen Support Programme for Ukraine - HUM - international partners;B;2025;01.10.2025;Planned;9 000 000;0;;2022;2026;UNICEF;;300540;UKR-NANSEN Avdeling for Nansen-programmet for Ukraina;0159;0159.73;0159.73.112;Humanitær bistand;Ukraine;NORAD-TAKV;Kvalvaag, Tale;2301989;03;;13.11.2023;UNICEF - United Nations Children's Fund;UNICEF - United Nations Children's Fund;United Nations;I(S);Project- and programme grant - with subunits;Earmarked to multilaterals;Contributions to multi-donor/single-entity funding mechanisms;72010;720;Emergency Response;10;Material relief assistance and services;;-;-;-;-;-;-;-;-;-;-;-;-;-;-;-;-;As per UNICEF's HAC for Ukraine, ssupporting unaccompanied ad separated children, preventing human trafficking and locating children i state custody will remain priorities, along with case management for children returning from boarding institutions or in alternative care arrangements. ;;
SM;RER-23/0013-1;Humanitarian response Ukraine - NORCAP;QZA-1032;The Nansen Support Programme for Ukraine - HUM - Norwegian partners;D;2025;10.09.2025;Actual;- 1 006 525;0;NOK;2022;2025;Flyktninghjelpen;Grant;300540;UKR-NANSEN Avdeling for Nansen-programmet for Ukraina;0159;0159.73;0159.73.112;Humanitær bistand;Ukraine;NORAD-U1257;Randa, Trond Inge;;03;;21.11.2023;Flyktninghjelpen;Flyktninghjelpen;NGO Norwegian;I(S);Project- and programme grant - with subunits;Bilateral;Donor country personnel;72010;720;Emergency Response;10;Material relief assistance and services;;-;-;1;-;-;-;-;-;-;-;-;-;-;-;-;-;In 2024 NORCAP will continue supporting agencies and governments to provide basic humanitarian needs for the people affected by the war in Ukraine. NORCAP will continue supporting and expanding its area of interventions in protection from sexual and gender-based violence, education, clean energy, Cash and Community Engagement and Accountability and localisation in Ukraine and the neighbouring countries. Experts deployed to Ukraine and the neighbouring countries will support various stakeholders on technical issues, will contribute to quality programme design and coordinate/harmonise humanitarian responses. With the objective to build sustainable structure these experts will also build capacity of their counterparts, ensure that learnings are captured, analysed and disseminated across accordingly. ;;Satisfactory
S;RER-23/0014-1;UNHCR Humanitarian Support to Ukraine;QZA-1033;The Nansen Support Programme for Ukraine - HUM - international partners;B;2025;15.04.2025;Actual;530 000 000;0;NOK;2022;2026;UNHCR Voluntary Funds;Grant;300540;UKR-NANSEN Avdeling for Nansen-programmet for Ukraina;0159;0159.73;0159.73.112;Humanitær bistand;Ukraine;NORAD-VIH;Halvorsen, Vigdis;2301957;03;;04.12.2023;UNHCR - UN Office of the UN High Commissioner for Refugees;UNHCR - UN Office of the UN High Commissioner for Refugees;United Nations;II(S);General funding grant - with subunits;Earmarked to multilaterals;Contributions to multi-donor/single-entity funding mechanisms;72010;720;Emergency Response;10;Material relief assistance and services;;-;-;1;-;-;-;Significant;-;-;-;-;-;-;-;-;Significant;Support to UNHCR's humanitarian support to Ukraine within the 2023 Supplementary Appeal for the Ukraine situation. The assistance includes provision of protection services and information

;;
S;RER-24/0008-1;Humanitarian response Ukraine ;QZA-1032;The Nansen Support Programme for Ukraine - HUM - Norwegian partners;B;2025;07.10.2025;Actual;114 000 000;0;NOK;2024;2027;Norges Røde Kors;Grant;300540;UKR-NANSEN Avdeling for Nansen-programmet for Ukraina;0159;0159.73;0159.73.112;Humanitær bistand;Ukraine;NORAD-VIH;Halvorsen, Vigdis;;03;;19.12.2024;Norges Røde Kors;Norges Røde Kors;NGO Norwegian;I(S);Project- and programme grant - with subunits;Bilateral;Project-type interventions;72010;720;Emergency Response;10;Material relief assistance and services;;-;-;1;-;-;-;-;-;-;-;-;-;-;-;-;Significant;People affected by the war in Ukraine have improved health, resilience, and protection, through Ukrainian Red Cross as a strong, efficient, and leading humanitarian actor. Vulnerable and conflict affected people have improved access to quality health care.;;
S;RER-24/0009-1;Humanitarian response in Ukraine ;QZA-1032;The Nansen Support Programme for Ukraine - HUM - Norwegian partners;B;2025;26.08.2025;Actual;124 187 987;0;NOK;2024;2027;Flyktninghjelpen;Grant;300540;UKR-NANSEN Avdeling for Nansen-programmet for Ukraina;0159;0159.73;0159.73.112;Humanitær bistand;Ukraine;NORAD-VIH;Halvorsen, Vigdis;;03;;17.12.2024;Flyktninghjelpen;Flyktninghjelpen;NGO Norwegian;I(S);Project- and programme grant - with subunits;Bilateral;Project-type interventions;72010;720;Emergency Response;10;Material relief assistance and services;;-;-;1;-;-;-;Significant;-;-;-;-;-;-;-;-;Significant;Humanitarian response in Ukraine. NRC is proposing a multisectoral response to the Ukraine crisis working in acute emergencies to situations of more protracted displacement and early recovery. The following programmatic interventions are included: Education, Information Counselling, Legal Assistance (ICLA), Shelter, WASH, Livelihoods and Food Security, Protection from Violence (PfV), Emergency Response. Two of the main modalities will be cash assistance and working with local partners.  NRC will target displacement-affected communities such as Internally Displaced Persons (IDPs) and returnees . NRC will prioritise services for the most vulnerable including single-headed families, most often women, the elderly, youth and minority communities, families with members who are sick or have disabilities, large families, and households unable to meet their basic needs.;;
S;RER-24/0009-2;Humanitarian response Moldova;QZA-1032;The Nansen Support Programme for Ukraine - HUM - Norwegian partners;B;2025;26.08.2025;Actual;29 907 692;0;NOK;2024;2027;Flyktninghjelpen;Grant;300540;UKR-NANSEN Avdeling for Nansen-programmet for Ukraina;0159;0159.73;0159.73.112;Humanitær bistand;Moldova;NORAD-VIH;Halvorsen, Vigdis;;03;;17.12.2024;Flyktninghjelpen;Flyktninghjelpen;NGO Norwegian;I(S);Project- and programme grant - with subunits;Bilateral;Project-type interventions;72010;720;Emergency Response;10;Material relief assistance and services;;-;-;-;-;1;-;-;-;-;-;-;-;-;-;-;Significant;Humanitarian response in Moldova. NRC is proposing a multisectoral response to the Ukraine crisis working in acute emergencies to situations of more protracted displacement and early recovery. The following programmatic interventions are included: Education, Information Counselling, Legal Assistance (ICLA), Shelter, WASH, Livelihoods and Food Security, Protection from Violence (PfV), Emergency Response. Two of the main modalities will be cash assistance and working with local partners.  NRC will target displacement-affected communities such as refugees from Ukraine, and households directly impacted by the conflict in host communities in Moldova. NRC will prioritise services for the most vulnerable including single-headed families, the elderly, youth and minority communities, families with members who are sick or have disabilities, large families, and households unable to meet their basic needs.  ;;
S;RER-24/0009-3;Humanitarian response in Poland ;QZA-1032;The Nansen Support Programme for Ukraine - HUM - Norwegian partners;B;2025;26.08.2025;Actual;3 030 475;0;NOK;2024;2027;Flyktninghjelpen;Grant;300540;UKR-NANSEN Avdeling for Nansen-programmet for Ukraina;0159;0159.73;0159.73.112;Humanitær bistand;Global Unspecified;NORAD-VIH;Halvorsen, Vigdis;;03;;17.12.2024;Flyktninghjelpen;Flyktninghjelpen;NGO Norwegian;I(S);Project- and programme grant - with subunits;Bilateral;Refugees and asylum seekers in other provider countries;93010;930;Refugees in donor countries;10;Refugees in donor countries;;-;-;-;-;-;-;-;-;-;-;-;-;-;-;-;-;Humanitarian response to ukrainian refugees in Poland. NRC is proposing a multisectoral response to the Ukraine crisis working in acute emergencies to situations of more protracted displacement and early recovery. The following programmatic interventions are included: Education, Information Counselling, Legal Assistance (ICLA), Shelter, WASH, Livelihoods and Food Security, Protection from Violence (PfV), Emergency Response. Two of the main modalities will be cash assistance and working with local partners.  NRC will target displacement-affected communities such as refugees from Ukraine, and households directly impacted by the conflict in host communities in Poland. NRC will prioritise services for the most vulnerable including single-headed families, the elderly, youth and minority communities, families with members who are sick or have disabilities, large families, and households unable to meet their basic needs.;STAT: Flyktningutgifter i giverland kan ikke markeres med policymarkører og flyktningmarkører.;
S;RER-24/0009-4;Flexible funding in the context of multisectoral response to the Ukraine crisis.;QZA-1032;The Nansen Support Programme for Ukraine - HUM - Norwegian partners;B;2025;26.08.2025;Actual;22 873 846;0;NOK;2024;2027;Flyktninghjelpen;Grant;300540;UKR-NANSEN Avdeling for Nansen-programmet for Ukraina;0159;0159.73;0159.73.112;Humanitær bistand;Europe Regional;NORAD-VIH;Halvorsen, Vigdis;;03;;17.12.2024;Flyktninghjelpen;Flyktninghjelpen;NGO Norwegian;I(S);Project- and programme grant - with subunits;Bilateral;Project-type interventions;72010;720;Emergency Response;10;Material relief assistance and services;;-;-;1;-;1;-;-;-;-;-;-;-;-;-;-;-;Flexible share of funding for the Norwegian Refugee Council (Flyktninghjelpen) in the context of multisectoral response to the Ukraine crisis.;;
SM;RER-24/0010-1;Deployment of experts to Ukraine ;QZA-1032;The Nansen Support Programme for Ukraine - HUM - Norwegian partners;B;2025;10.09.2025;Actual;1 006 525;0;NOK;2024;2027;Flyktninghjelpen;Grant;300540;UKR-NANSEN Avdeling for Nansen-programmet for Ukraina;0159;0159.73;0159.73.112;Humanitær bistand;Ukraine;NORAD-U1257;Randa, Trond Inge;;03;;17.12.2024;Flyktninghjelpen;Flyktninghjelpen;NGO Norwegian;I(S);Project- and programme grant - with subunits;Bilateral;Project-type interventions;72010;720;Emergency Response;10;Material relief assistance and services;;-;-;1;-;-;-;Significant;-;-;-;-;-;-;-;-;-;NORCAP will continue supporting agencies and governments to provide basic humanitarian needs for the people affected by the war in Ukraine. NORCAP will continue supporting and expanding its area of interventions in protection from sexual and gender-based violence, education, clean energy, Cash and Community Engagement and Accountability and localisation in Ukraine and the neighbouring countries. Experts deployed to Ukraine and the neighbouring countries will support various stakeholders on technical issues, will contribute to quality programme design and coordinate/harmonise humanitarian responses. With the objective to build sustainable structure these experts will also build capacity of their counterparts, ensure that learnings are captured, analysed and disseminated across accordingly.;;
