;RER-25/0016;BREnDA - Accelerating Decarbonisation and Energy Security in W Balkans;SRB-0017;Embassy managed projects;B;2025;07.08.2025;Actual;1 500 000;0;NOK;2025;2026;Fondacija BFPE za odgovorno drustvo;Grant;4080;Beograd;0159;0159.71;0159.71.111;Europa/Vest-Balkan;Europe Regional;NEJO;Jovic, Nela;25/4039;03;;29.07.2025;BFPE - Belgrade Fund for Political Ecellence;BFPE - Belgrade Fund for Political Ecellence;NGO Local;I;Project- and programme grant;Bilateral;Contributions to specific-purpose programmes and funds managed by implementing partners;23270;232;Energy generation, renewable sources;70;Biofuel-fired power plants;;-;-;-;-;-;Significant;-;-;-;Significant;-;-;-;-;-;-;This pilot project supports the development of a concept – Balkan Renewable Energy Accelerator (BREnDA), which will consist of a viable Framework Investment Plan (FIP) for decarbonising the Western Balkans’ heat and power sector by identifying investment-ready projects and engaging local public utilities, private investors, and technology providers. It aims to strengthen energy security, promote cleaner technologies, and lay the groundwork for a more sustainable and resilient regional energy system.;;
