;SAF-23/0001;Lfu - SSB Food Security statistics 2024-2027;QZA-1009;Landbruk for utvikling - Lfu ;B;2025;30.11.2025;Planned;3 940 203;0;;2024;2027;Statistisk Sentralbyrå;;300512;KNN-MAT Seksjon for mat;0162;0162.71;0162.71.113;Landbruk for utvikling;South of Sahara Regional;NORAD-U12773;Dypedokk, Kristin;2301621;03;;07.12.2023;SSB - Statistisk Sentralbyrå;SSB - Statistisk Sentralbyrå;Norwegian public sector;I;Project- and programme grant;Bilateral;Other technical assistance;43071;430;Other multisector;71;Food security policy and administrative management;Kunnskapsbanken;-;-;-;-;-;-;-;Significant;-;Significant;-;-;-;-;Significant;-;The overall project goal in the project proposed here is improved food security situation in low- and middle-income countries. The contribution to this is that more statistics is produced from household surveys and used for better policies and implementation of concrete projects.The Norwegian Bureau of statistics will collaborate with COMESA and some national institutions  with a strong element of capacity development. This will include increased knowledge of how to process household budget survey  data so they are accessible to food security indicators and increased knowledge on how to use this data in multiple types of analysis. The support is a part of the Agriculture for development program. Correct data on food security and food consumption is important input for the authorities as well as development partners when assessing if – and what sort of interventions should be implemented to avoid or reduce food insecurity.;Videreføring av SAF-20/0003;
S;SAF-23/0002-1;Food vocational training - WE4D Employment Promotion for Women for Green Transformation in Africa;QZA-0719;Enhancing job relevant skills for youth and young adults;B;2025;20.06.2025;Actual;3 099 389;0;NOK;2023;2027;Deutsche Gesellschaft für Internationale Zusammenarbeit(GIZ) GmbH;Grant;300523;VEM-UTFORSK Seksjon for utdanning og forskning;0161;0161.70;0161.70.124;Yrkesopplæring;South of Sahara Regional;NORAD-U15131;Torskenæs, Helga;2300607;03;Africa regional (Reg. Afrika);04.12.2023;GIZ - Deutsche Gesellschaft fur Internationale Zusammenarbeit;GIZ - Deutsche Gesellschaft fur Internationale Zusammenarbeit;Public sector other donor countries;I(S);Project- and programme grant - with subunits;Bilateral;Project-type interventions;31181;311;Agriculture;81;Agricultural education and training;;-;-;-;-;-;Significant;Main;-;-;-;-;Significant;-;-;-;Significant;The aim of WE4D is to improve the employment and economic situation of women in Africa, especially in companies and sectors that promote the green transformation of the economy. The programme is implemented in the following fields of action: (1) labour market-oriented education and training, (2) transition to the labour market, (3) employment in value chains, (4) competitiveness of start-ups and MSMEs and (5) regional scaling of approaches. To promote the green transformation, WE4D focuses on green sectors (Sustainable Agriculture/ Agroprocessing, Circular Economy/ Waste Management/ Biomass, Eco-Tourism, Blue Economy and Aquaculture, Renewable Energy) and conventional sectors with a potential for greening (Construction, Transport and Logistics).  Persons with disabilities (PwD) are among the target groups of the project. The programme will be implemented in six countries: Kenya, Malawi, Mozambique, South Africa, Tanzania, and Uganda. ;;
