;SOM-24/0002;Environmental Peacemaking in Somalia II;SOM-2021;Peace, reconciliation and democratisation in Somalia;B;2025;01.07.2025;Actual;1 750 000;0;NOK;2025;2027;European Institute of Peace;Grant;4490;Nairobi/Kenya;0159;0159.75;0159.75.111;Afrika - nasjonale tiltak;Somalia;MKOM;Komen, Margaret;;03;;26.06.2025;EIP - European Institute of Peace;EIP - European Institute of Peace;NGO International;I;Project- and programme grant;Bilateral;Project-type interventions;41010;410;General environmental protection;10;Environmental policy and administrative management;;-;-;-;-;-;Main;Significant;-;-;-;-;-;Significant;-;-;-;The overall objective is to improve relationships and dialogue between the Federal Government of Somalia and four Federal Member States over environmental governance, as well as support international partners with strategic research on environmental peace-making topics to enhance environmental governance, to contribute to conflict resolution and prevention in Somalia. The project focuses on three target groups, first Somali FGS and FMS actors with environmental mandates. Second, Somali FGS and FMS actors working on interior, justice and security. And third, international actors working on environment, climate peace and security in Somalia.;;
;SOM-24/0002;Environmental Peacemaking in Somalia II;SOM-2021;Peace, reconciliation and democratisation in Somalia;B;2025;18.11.2025;Actual;1 750 000;0;NOK;2025;2027;European Institute of Peace;Grant;4490;Nairobi/Kenya;0159;0159.75;0159.75.111;Afrika - nasjonale tiltak;Somalia;MKOM;Komen, Margaret;;03;;26.06.2025;EIP - European Institute of Peace;EIP - European Institute of Peace;NGO International;I;Project- and programme grant;Bilateral;Project-type interventions;41010;410;General environmental protection;10;Environmental policy and administrative management;;-;-;-;-;-;Main;Significant;-;-;-;-;-;Significant;-;-;-;The overall objective is to improve relationships and dialogue between the Federal Government of Somalia and four Federal Member States over environmental governance, as well as support international partners with strategic research on environmental peace-making topics to enhance environmental governance, to contribute to conflict resolution and prevention in Somalia. The project focuses on three target groups, first Somali FGS and FMS actors with environmental mandates. Second, Somali FGS and FMS actors working on interior, justice and security. And third, international actors working on environment, climate peace and security in Somalia.;;
