;TUR-24/0012;Amnesty- Enhancing Child Rights-Based Approaches Through an Intersectional Perspective  ;TUR-1009;Human Rights;B;2025;30.04.2025;Actual;445 694;0;NOK;2024;2026;Uluslararasi AF Orgutu Turkiye Subesi;Grant;4020;Ankara;0152;0152.70;0152.70.111;Menneskerettigheter;Turkey;U18474;Yücedag, Deniz;;03;;03.09.2024;Amnesty International - local office;Amnesty International - local office;NGO Local;I;Project- and programme grant;Bilateral;Project-type interventions;15160;151;Government and civil society, general;60;Human rights;;-;-;-;-;-;-;Significant;Main;-;-;-;-;-;-;-;-;The main objective of the project is is for individuals/professionals or prospective professionals working with children who participated in Dilek Kumcu Child Rights Programme to  have enhanced knowledge, awareness, and skills on children’ human rights through an intersectional perspective predominantly focusing on gender equality;;
