;TUR-24/0013;NHC- Advocates for Change: Türkiye Civil Society Program 2024/2025;TUR-1009;Human Rights;C;2025;18.03.2025;Actual;1 695 593;0;NOK;2024;2025;Den Norske Helsingforskomite;Grant;4020;Ankara;0152;0152.70;0152.70.111;Menneskerettigheter;Turkey;U18474;Yücedag, Deniz;24/8818;03;;05.09.2024;Den norske helsingforskomiteen;Den norske helsingforskomiteen;NGO Norwegian;I;Project- and programme grant;Bilateral;Project-type interventions;15160;151;Government and civil society, general;60;Human rights;;-;-;-;-;-;-;Significant;Main;-;-;-;-;-;-;-;-;The main objective of the project is to build capacity of small society organizations in Turkey, including mentorship. The focus areas are protection of human rights, democratic principals, and the rule of law. More concreately, this includes focusing on human rights defenders, freedom of expression and the media, LGBTQIA+, gender equality and women empowerement. The project aims at reaching organizations outside of the big cities of Ankara, Istanbul and Izmir.;;
;TUR-25/0001;New: Now Exhibition;TUR-1012;Culture, press, corporations and promotion;D;2025;24.04.2025;Actual;3 300;0;NOK;2025;2025;Target Dis Ticaret Turizm Ltd Sti;Grant;4020;Ankara;0115;0115.70;0115.70.112;Kultur- og informasjonsformål - ute/stasjonene;Turkey;U16593;Yilmaz, Benan Bilun;;02;;07.04.2025;Undefined (Target Dis Ticaret Turizm Ltd Sti);Undefined (Target Dis Ticaret Turizm Ltd Sti);Private sector in developing countries;III;Small-scale grant;Bilateral;Other technical assistance;16061;160;Other social infrastructure and services;61;Culture and cultural diversity;;-;-;-;-;-;-;-;-;-;-;-;-;-;-;-;-;The New:Now, Second Edition exhibition, curated by Attila Güllü, highlights the work of young, talented artists in CerModern Main Hall. This event will provide important exposure for emerging artists and strengthen their presence in the art community. The planned results include an exhibition that showcases new artistic talent and increases public engagement. The overall goal is to support young artists and promote their work to a wider audience. The Norwegian participation will be three photography works of Marcus Reistad which will help promoting Norwegian contemporary artists in Turkiye. ;;Satisfactory
;TUR-25/0002;Istanbul Film Festival 2025;TUR-1012;Culture, press, corporations and promotion;D;2025;22.04.2025;Actual;20 000;0;NOK;2025;2025;Istanbul Kultur Sanat Vakfi;Grant;4020;Ankara;0115;0115.70;0115.70.112;Kultur- og informasjonsformål - ute/stasjonene;Turkey;U16593;Yilmaz, Benan Bilun;;02;;04.04.2025;IKSV - Istanbul Foundation for Culture and Arts;IKSV - Istanbul Foundation for Culture and Arts;NGO Local;III;Small-scale grant;Bilateral;Other technical assistance;16061;160;Other social infrastructure and services;61;Culture and cultural diversity;;-;-;-;-;-;-;-;-;-;-;-;-;-;-;-;-;The 44th Edition of Istanbul Film Festival will host a retrospective section dedicated to Dag Johan Haugerud's films. Six of Haugerud's films 'Dreams', 'Love', 'Sex', 'The Light from the Chocolate Factory', 'Beware of Children', 'I Belong' will be screened at the festival. Haugerud himself will also attend for artist talks. ;;Satisfactory
;TUR-25/0003;Ankara International Wildlife Documentary Film Festival;TUR-1012;Culture, press, corporations and promotion;D;2025;24.04.2025;Actual;10 000;0;NOK;2025;2025;Doga Koruma Merkezi Vakfi;Grant;4020;Ankara;0115;0115.70;0115.70.112;Kultur- og informasjonsformål - ute/stasjonene;Turkey;U16593;Yilmaz, Benan Bilun;;02;;08.04.2025;Undefined (Nature Conservation Centre (DKM));Undefined (Nature Conservation Centre (DKM));NGO Local;III;Small-scale grant;Bilateral;Other technical assistance;16061;160;Other social infrastructure and services;61;Culture and cultural diversity;;-;-;-;-;-;-;-;-;-;-;-;-;-;-;-;-;Ankara International Wildlife Documentary Film Festival aims to introduce the best of wildlife films and their makers to Turkish audience and to increase the public awareness on the changing environment and what is at stake. While the target audience is the general public, the festival does pay a special importance to the young audience both in taking part in the festival as volunteers and attending to festival talks and screenings as the policy makers of the future. The participation from Norway will be with the film “A Call from the Wild” and the attendance of its director Asgeir Helgestad and producer Angeliki Lefkaditou, where Turkish wildlife filmmakers will have the chance to directly listen to their experiences. ;;Satisfactory
