;UKR-24/0012;International Transport Forum ITF CIG4U Common Interest Group for Ukraine;UKR-0015;Belastningsfullmakt Samferdselsdepartementet;B;2025;01.09.2025;Planned;3 000 000;0;;2024;2025;OECD;;410401;Øst-Europaseksjonen;0159;0159.73;0159.73.111;Ukraina og naboland;Ukraine;BHK;Kjølås, Britt Hilde;24/12889;03;;05.12.2024;OECD - Organisation for Economic Co-operation and Development;OECD - Organisation for Economic Co-operation and Development;Other multilateral institutions;II;General funding grant;Earmarked to multilaterals;Contributions to multi-donor/single-entity funding mechanisms;21010;210;Transport and storage;10;Transport policy and administrative management;;-;-;-;-;-;-;-;-;-;-;-;-;-;-;-;-;The International Transport Forum at the OECD is an intergovernmental organisation with 60 member countries. It acts as a think tank for transport policy and organises the Annual Summit of transport ministers. ITF is the only global body that covers all transport modes. The ITF is administratively integrated with the OECD

