;UKR-24/0051;IDEA - Ukrainians Voting: Organizing Trustworthy Elections (U-VOTE);UKR-0016;Ukraine Democracy Human Rights Transparency;A;2025;28.02.2025;Planned;30 000 000;0;;2025;2026;International Idea;;300540;UKR-NANSEN Avdeling for Nansen-programmet for Ukraina;0159;0159.73;0159.73.111;Ukraina og naboland;Ukraine;NORAD-U14828;Bugge, Tuva Grimsæth;2502926;03;;;IDEA - International Institute for Democracy and Electoral Assistance;IDEA - International Institute for Democracy and Electoral Assistance;Other multilateral institutions;I;Project- and programme grant;Earmarked to multilaterals;Contributions to single-donor funding mechanisms and contributions earmarked for a specific funding window or geographical locat;15151;151;Government and civil society, general;51;Elections;;-;-;-;-;-;-;Significant;Main;-;-;-;-;-;-;-;-;The U-VOTE (Ukrainians Voting: Organizing Trustworthy Elections) programme, implemented by International IDEA, supports Ukraine’s preparation for credible, inclusive, and secure post-war elections. Working with the Central Election Commission, Verkhovna Rada, NACP, and civil society, the project strengthens electoral integrity, cybersecurity, transparency in political finance, and voter participation. It contributes to the governance, public sector capacity, and gender equality sectors. Gender and inclusion are mainstreamed, ensuring participation of women, youth, displaced persons, and veterans. U-VOTE enhances democratic resilience and supports Ukraine’s path toward accountable, European-aligned governance.;;
