;UKR-25/0017;UNDP - ACCELERATING THE GREEN TRANSITION IN UKRAINE;UKR-0005;Energy reform and -efficiency;B;2025;15.08.2025;Actual;1 500 000;0;NOK;2025;2027;UNDP Contributions;Grant;300540;UKR-NANSEN Avdeling for Nansen-programmet for Ukraina;0159;0159.73;0159.73.111;Ukraina og naboland;Ukraine;NORAD-U18138;Kyryliuk, Anatolii;2501047;03;;10.07.2025;UNDP - UN Development Programme;UNDP - UN Development Programme;United Nations;I;Project- and programme grant;Earmarked to multilaterals;Contributions to multi-donor/single-entity funding mechanisms;23110;231;Energy Policy;10;Energy policy and administrative management;;-;-;-;-;-;Main;-;Significant;-;-;-;-;-;-;-;-;This UNDP initiative under the Green Energy Recovery Programme focuses on strengthening Ukraine’s capacity for a green transition. It supports regulatory reforms to unlock investments in decentralized, sustainable energy and advocates for a competitive heat market by enabling third-party access and unbundling monopolistic structures. The project also promotes financial empowerment of women-led green businesses through tailored financial instruments and partnerships with national development platforms.Together, these efforts aim to foster inclusive, resilient, and market-driven energy reform in Ukraine.;;
