;UKR-25/0026;UNICEF Reintegration of Children and MoJ Ukraine;QZA-1033;The Nansen Support Programme for Ukraine - HUM - international partners;B;2025;18.09.2025;Actual;10 000 000;0;NOK;2025;2027;UNICEF;Grant;300540;UKR-NANSEN Avdeling for Nansen-programmet for Ukraina;0159;0159.73;0159.73.112;Humanitær bistand;Ukraine;NORAD-U18919;Dibb, Rebecca Volckmar;;03;Protection (incl. Child Protection and SGBV);22.08.2025;UNICEF - United Nations Children's Fund;UNICEF - United Nations Children's Fund;United Nations;I;Project- and programme grant;Bilateral;Project-type interventions;15160;151;Government and civil society, general;60;Human rights;;-;-;-;-;-;-;-;-;-;-;-;-;-;-;-;-;This project works with UNICEF to support their child protection work in Ukraine. Specfically this project aims to support UNICEF's work in supporting the Ministry of Justice in Ukraine in their work on the reintegration of children who have returned after being deported. UNICEF has extensive expertise in working on child protection and provides an advisory as well as technical role in this project where the main component is to set up and modernise a database to ensure there is a way to ensure consistent case management and follow-up of these children. The database will be modernised and staff and users will be trained to ensure it is used and implemented. The database allows practiioners across the social security system in Ukraine to be able to give ;This is a project that builds on UNICEF's child protection work to ensure children who have been forcibly deported from Ukraine are safely returned to Ukraine. This project will specifically work with the Ministry of Justice in Ukraine to support them in moderninsing and formally establish a database/ register of deported children and ensure their reintegration journey is properly managed through this database. The database ensures a holistic approach to their case management and allows for targeted service provision specific to each of the children once they return to Ukraine. UNICEF brings both technological support and their expertise in child protection to ensure the database is set up in the best way as well as being user-friendly. ;
